WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.801
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.902
happening all the time,

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.871
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.073
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.442
ELF has been killing it with
its new releases lately,

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.745
and we need to talk about
this new Power Grip Primer,

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.413
because it's excellent.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.781
Immediately I compared it

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.349
to my Milk Hydro Grip Primer.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.518
They are virtually identical

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.854
in terms of texture and how they apply,

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.757
except this ELF one is obviously cheaper.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.058
Just like the Hydro Grip Primer,

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.827
it creates a really nice
tacky base for foundation

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.963
that's meant to make
your makeup last longer.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.565
My foundation blended out
really nicely on top of this.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.466
It wasn't pilling

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.402
or doing anything out of the ordinary.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.336
I took some pictures

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.371
about five to six hours after I applied,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.540
and I do think my makeup
lasted really well,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.374
even my blush,

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.909
which is literally always the first thing

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.244
to disappear on my face.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.479
ELF also released this powder foundation

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.647
in its Camo line.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.149
I'll be honest: Powder foundations

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.217
are just not my thing.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.819
I don't like how they look on my skin,

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.654
but the Camo line has
had nothing but hits,

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:55.989
so I had to try this.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.590
The powder is so soft,

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.392
and it blends out very easily.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.127
It definitely evened out my skin tone

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:04.464
and blurred some of those
areas I have of discoloration.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.100
However, it just looks powdery!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.635
I don't think it gives my skin

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.403
the most flattering texture.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.838
I forgot to set it with some spray

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.006
to see if that helps at all,

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.974
but I don't see myself liking this,

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:17.243
even with setting spray
to melt it in a bit.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.845
This is not for me.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.814
I love trying new mascaras.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:23.850
This is the Makeup Revolution
5D Lash Pow Mascara.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.118
It's supposed to make it look like

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.419
you're wearing falsies.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:29.222
The size of this brush is astronomical.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.056
Oh, my God.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.626
But I love a big
natural-bristle mascara brush.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.494
Right away, I could tell

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.396
that this mascara was
doing a really nice job

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.897
of thickening my lashes.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.898
And the more I built it up,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.034
it gave my lashes this nice little curl.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.036
I naturally have straight lashes,

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.370
and I hate curling them,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.872
so I was really happy with the effect

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.107
this mascara gave them.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.676
Also, I love how you push
the cap down to open it.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.111
It's really satisfying to me.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.446
The Fenty Beauty Killawatt
Freestyle Highlighter

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.948
is definitely not new,

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.083
but Madison Beer said she uses this one

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.386
in Ginger Binge/Moscow Mule as a blush,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.689
and everyone bought it, including me.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.425
Fenty highlighters are
more glittery than sheeny,

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.559
so I was a little nervous

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.128
about how this was going to look on me

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.063
and the texture on my cheeks.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.031
It was definitely more metallic-looking,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.234
because it's a highlighter
and not a blush,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.169
but I actually did not hate this at all.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.104
I did have to go over it with my sponge

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.439
to take away some of that glitter,

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.574
but the color and the glow
it brought to my cheeks

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.575
was super pretty.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.344
I don't think you need
this specific product

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.445
for this kind of effect,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.346
but if you're going to try it,

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.781
I recommend sticking to
the side with less glitter.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.049
Charlotte Tilbury just dropped

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.618
this Beautiful Skin Foundation.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.486
The claims on the box were so funny to me.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:37.924
Like, "skin tone looks more
even by up to 210%" ...

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:38.758
sure.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.860
This foundation had a
way thicker consistency

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.896
than I expected, and I
think because of that,

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.631
it didn't really melt into my skin

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.266
the way I wanted it to.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.067
The coverage leaned more
on the lighter side,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.836
so I went back into certain areas

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.037
and added some more.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.405
It's definitely buildable,

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:55.008
but I'm not obsessed with
how my skin is looking.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.543
I don't think it looks cakey,

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.244
it just looks like I'm wearing foundation,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.579
and it's not as skin-like

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.247
as the name would have you think.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.216
Do I think my skin tone looks more even

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.418
by up to 210%?

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.786
I can't really say,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.288
but this is just OK to me.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:11.024
I saw a TikTok that said
this Sigma Renew Lip Oil

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:14.027
is a possible dupe for
the $35 Dior lip oil,

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.395
so I had to compare the two,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.198
because I am obsessed
with the Dior lip oil.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.999
It feels so nourishing on the lips,

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.135
and it has that big doe-foot applicator

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.503
that feels so cushiony.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.438
I could literally apply this all day.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.840
The Sigma lip oil looks so much like it.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.008
Look at these applicators.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.510
They're almost identical.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.545
The Sigma one is hydrating and shiny,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.315
and it gives you that
moisturizing, non-sticky feeling.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.383
It feels so much like the Dior one.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.851
The only discernible difference

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.986
I found between the two

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.788
is that the Sigma one has no scent,

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.289
and the Dior one does.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.726
It's $22, which is still
really pricey for a lip oil,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.194
and it only comes in four shades,

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.696
but I think this is a really good dupe.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.297
Highly recommend.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.699
You guys have been asking me to try out

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.967
some Rare Beauty on this show,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.001
so I picked up the new

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.803
Warm Wishes Effortless Bronzer Stick

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.137
and the Always an Optimist

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.839
Soft Radiance Setting Powder.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.908
Let's talk about the bronzer stick first.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.243
I immediately got nervous

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.644
swatching it on the back of my hand,

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.980
because it looked so red.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.947
But I was so shocked

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.682
when I saw how easily it blended in.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:10.850
I don't know why I applied this

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.051
like it was a contour stick,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.219
but it worked out for me.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.588
The texture of this is something special.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:18.191
It's super smooth and soft and velvety,

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.959
and it doesn't blend into nothing.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.427
You still see that color.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.529
You still get the warmth of a bronzer.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:24.731
It looked way less red

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.898
when I applied it to my face,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.201
so I was actually really happy with this.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.469
Now the setting powder.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.536
I'll admit right now,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.505
I made a mistake getting the medium shade.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.240
I should've gone for light medium,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.276
but I expected this to be way more sheer

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.644
than it actually was.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.512
I normally use a translucent powder,

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.281
so using a setting powder with color

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.448
was new for me.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.051
Applying it with my sponge
was an immediate no.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:48.087
It made my skin look so patchy and weird.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.657
My powder brush was
definitely the way to go.

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.358
The powder was super-finely milled,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.926
and it gives your skin that soft blur

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.261
that looks really pretty.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.330
It made my skin look a
lot smoother on the side

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.431
where I used my brush.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.633
It's still a little
patchy in terms of color,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.268
but that's obviously my fault,

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.936
because this is not my color.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.538
I definitely need to try this again

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.140
in my appropriate shade.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.608
And finally, let's talk about

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.810
the new NYX Thick It. Stick It! Brow Gel.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.246
It's described as a
thickening brow mascara.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.380
If you look really closely,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.848
you can see those little fibers

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.116
that are supposed to make your brows

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.718
look fuller and fluffier.

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.453
I actually bought this for myself

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.889
and used it once and
thought it was just OK,

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.224
but I had no idea you
were supposed to layer it.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.659
So I did that this time around,

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.861
and my brows came out so much better.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.863
I'm obsessed with how
this right brow looks.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.465
The left one, not so much,

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.100
but that's always my problem brow.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.768
I kind of wish this had a smaller brush,

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.837
because I kept accidentally
spreading the product

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.372
outside of my brows.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.507
But I do like the natural full effect

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.642
that you get with this.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:45.144
I haven't tried a Hard Candy
product since I was a kid,

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.513
but this glitter palette
blew up on TikTok.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.682
This is the Glitteratzi
glitter eye palette

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.217
in Glitz N' Cheer.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.552
The glitter is not loose.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.387
It does have some sort of sticky base

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.488
that holds it together

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.557
and makes it really easy to glide on.

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:58.725
I was honestly blown away

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.493
by how pigmented these glitters are.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:03.096
I used my fingers to apply it to my eyes.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:05.164
These top two shades do that thing where

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.966
depending on what angle your face is at,

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.035
the glitter disappears and reappears.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.970
It's so magical and pretty.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.039
I will say that I did get glitter fallout,

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.108
so I'd recommend using
another glitter base

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.676
to make sure that doesn't happen,

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.644
but I had fun playing
around with this palette.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.079
If you're someone who's into glitter,

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.314
I highly recommend it.

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.415
Fenty Beauty just came out

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.884
with the Icon semi-matte
refillable lipstick.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:28.087
So the case and the actual
lipstick are sold separately,

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.856
and then you assemble them together.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.858
I'm not gonna lie, it took
me a minute to figure out,

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.992
but I did eventually.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.494
I got the shade The MVP,

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.662
which is another universal red from Fenty

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.998
that's supposed to look
good on every skin tone.

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.900
The shape of the lipstick
was actually inspired

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.136
by Rihanna's iconic Cupid's bow,

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.504
and I actually found it really easy

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.272
to sort of map out my lip line with it,

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.441
since I didn't apply any lip liner before.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:51.344
The pigment is incredible
and totally full coverage.

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:53.079
It's just a very creamy formula

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.982
that feels so smooth and
hydrating on the lips.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.784
I can't even believe this is semi-matte.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.819
It's definitely not transfer-proof,

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:01.320
but I was actually really impressed

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.823
by how it looked after I kissed my hand.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.591
Clearly so much product came off,

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.226
but the lipstick still looked incredible.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:10.062
It is interesting to see
regular lipstick releases

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:11.697
in the age of mask wearing,

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.566
but this formula is excellent.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.401
NARS has a new foundation formula,

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:18.538
the Light Reflecting
Advanced Skincare foundation.

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:21.407
NARS knows how to do
complexion products so well,

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:22.909
and it has a huge hit with this.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.677
I've actually been using
this for weeks now,

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.245
and I'm completely in love with it.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.147
The foundation is so
lightweight on the skin.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.316
It feels like you're not
even wearing foundation.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.351
The coverage is on the
light to medium side,

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.020
but I definitely think you can build it up

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.421
without it getting cakey.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:36.756
The finish is so nice.

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.958
It makes your skin look
really fresh and dewy

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.226
without looking oily,

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:41.694
and all of my other products layer

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.596
on top of this foundation really well.

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.798
KVD Beauty released its Good Apple

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.733
lightweight full-coverage concealer.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.168
The name had me so intrigued,

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:51.003
because usually full-coverage products

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.405
can get heavy on the skin,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.474
and my under-eyes are so picky

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.175
about what concealer they like.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:58.411
I immediately love this applicator shape.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.012
It picks up a good amount of product,

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.914
and the shape makes it easy to apply.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:04.116
I could tell from testing it
out on the back of my hand

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.152
that it actually does
feel way more lightweight

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.488
than I expected, but
it covers really well.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:11.023
I applied it everywhere I
normally apply concealer,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.458
let it all sit for a second,

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.826
and then started blending.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.561
This concealer blends like a dream.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:18.564
It just melts into the skin
without losing any coverage.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:20.466
I did add a little more
on my under-eye area

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:21.901
just for some extra brightening,

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:24.203
and it layered beautifully,
no problems there,

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.671
and then I set it all with the powder,

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.240
and I think it still looked really good

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.342
while feeling super-light on the face.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.710
The name did not lie.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.211
Colourpop released these adorable

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:34.180
heart-shaped pressed-powder blushes

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.815
just in time for Valentine's Day.

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:37.683
They kept selling out,
but I managed to get

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:40.653
this bright coral shade
called 4Ever Yours.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:43.523
These blushes look
deceptively matte in the pan,

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:45.057
but if you look at my finger swatch,

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:47.460
it's definitely got a
pretty sheen, which I love.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.862
This blush was so unbelievably pigmented.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.898
I tapped my brush off before I applied it,

00:08:51.898 --> 00:08:53.933
and it still went on this intensely.

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:56.102
But I went back in with a
clean brush to tone it down,

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:57.370
and it looked so much better.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.072
This blush formula is
really silky and pretty,

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:02.708
plus a little goes a really
long way, so I love this.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.144
Also, I am a sucker for
anything heart-shaped.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:07.547
Karla Cosmetics is a
totally new brand for me,

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:08.848
and I've been dying to try its

00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:11.317
Shadow Potion gel eye shadow.

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.686
It's this multichrome gel eye shadow.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.121
I swatched it on my hand first,

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:18.057
and this texture isn't something
I've really tried before.

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:19.325
I just went in with my fingers

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.260
and did gentle tapping motions.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.563
It does dry quickly, but not so quickly

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.398
that you don't have time to work with it.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:28.501
It definitely showed up as
more pinky-purple on my eyes

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.603
with olive green on the outer corners.

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:32.572
That multichrome shift
depends on the lighting,

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:33.973
so I think it looked more obvious

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.409
away from direct sunlight.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:39.211
Milk Makeup recently
released this Rise mascara.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.147
I actually love their Kush mascara,

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:43.482
so I was really excited to try this,

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:44.984
and then I actually tried it.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:47.286
This is just so average.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.554
It took me three layers

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:51.023
for it to give my lashes any sort of lift,

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:52.892
and even that effect was subtle.

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:54.293
I've tried drugstore mascaras

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:56.562
that have done a lot more for a lot less.

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:58.965
This is the mini size,
and it was 14 bucks.

00:09:58.965 --> 00:10:01.000
I will say I did love the packaging.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.069
This material kind of
feels like a pencil grip,

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:04.170
and I love that.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.840
The actual mascara, not so much.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.676
This is the KimChi Chic
Beauty Teddy Kim palette

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:12.511
in the Boyfriend color story.

00:10:12.511 --> 00:10:14.947
It's an eye-shadow and face palette.

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:17.049
I went in with the blush
and highlighter first,

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:18.150
and I loved them.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.920
They were really buildable
and went on so smoothly.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.221
Moving on to the eye shadow,

00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:24.390
you do get a nice mix of mattes,

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.725
shimmers, and glitters.

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:28.361
I think all of these colors
work together really well.

00:10:28.361 --> 00:10:30.162
I went in with a couple of mattes first,

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.297
and they blended great.

00:10:31.297 --> 00:10:33.466
Then I played around with
these shimmers and glitters.

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:35.067
Again, these applied great.

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:36.736
They're super shiny and reflective,

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:38.471
but I did get fallout with the glitter,

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.239
so I recommend using a primer.

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:42.575
Overall, I was very
happy with this palette,

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:43.809
and another fun thing about it

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.611
is that it actually comes with stickers

00:10:45.611 --> 00:10:47.613
so you can customize your little bear.

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.749
My bear definitely goes
to "Euphoria" high.

00:10:49.749 --> 00:10:51.150
But, yes, I love this.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.019
I can see this being
really good for travel,

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:55.554
although maybe a little bit hard to pack.

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:57.857
This is the ELF Cookies
'n Dreams lip gloss

00:10:57.857 --> 00:10:58.824
in Cookie Dreams.

00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:01.060
And, yes, it is a black lip gloss

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.397
with a bunch of pretty blue
and silver glitter throughout.

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:06.499
I tried this out on my bare lips first,

00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:07.700
and I didn't love it

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.335
because you can see in the areas

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:11.537
where the gloss tends to pool a bit more,

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:14.106
it has this very obvious bluish-black tint

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:16.075
that looked a little odd on me.

00:11:16.075 --> 00:11:18.344
But then I applied this
over my favorite lip liner,

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:19.779
and I immediately understood

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:21.681
why people liked this so much.

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:24.417
Oh, my God, it looked
incredible over lip liner.

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.585
It kind of gave the liner a deeper look

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:28.387
that just worked so well.

00:11:28.387 --> 00:11:30.022
And the formula of the gloss itself

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:32.758
is actually really nice
for the $4 price point.

00:11:32.758 --> 00:11:34.427
I'm definitely hanging on to this

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:36.362
to layer over other lip products.

00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:39.331
The Rose Inc Skin Enhance
luminous tinted serum

00:11:39.331 --> 00:11:40.833
is one of the weirdest products

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:41.901
I've seen in a while.

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:45.571
It's basically a skin tint
with this serum-y base

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:47.139
that's filled with pigment beads

00:11:47.139 --> 00:11:49.008
that give you some coverage.

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:50.543
They say to apply this with a brush

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:52.611
to break up and spread
those pigment beads,

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:53.946
so that's what I did.

00:11:53.946 --> 00:11:55.247
I really went into this thinking

00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:57.349
it was just going to look
like an oily mess on me,

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:58.517
but then I noticed how good

00:11:58.517 --> 00:12:00.386
it was making my skin look.

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:01.754
The coverage is light,

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:03.589
but it's just enough that it gives this

00:12:03.589 --> 00:12:06.992
my-skin-naturally-looks-like-this-with-no-effort

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:07.993
kind of look.

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:10.596
I typically hide any
imperfections on my face

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:12.865
with a more full-coverage foundation,

00:12:12.865 --> 00:12:15.367
but this made my skin
look so smooth and dewy

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:17.636
that I didn't feel like I needed more.

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:19.338
But this product really shocked me,

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:20.940
not only in how good it looked

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.708
but also in how good it made me feel.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.310
I was so excited to try this

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.312
Huda Beauty Easy Bake loose baking

00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:28.581
and setting powder in Cherry Blossom.

00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:30.015
I had to get this baby version

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.384
because the full size
was completely sold out.

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.186
It's a baby pink setting powder

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:36.789
that's supposed to really
brighten up the under-eyes.

00:12:36.789 --> 00:12:38.791
I just applied my concealer like normal

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:40.092
and went in with the little puff

00:12:40.092 --> 00:12:42.094
that comes with it. This puff is nice,

00:12:42.094 --> 00:12:43.796
but the shape was really annoying to use,

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:44.864
so I did use a brush

00:12:44.864 --> 00:12:46.832
to get into the hard-to-reach spots.

00:12:46.832 --> 00:12:49.468
This powder does have a
very strong floral scent

00:12:49.468 --> 00:12:50.903
that was actually giving me a headache,

00:12:50.903 --> 00:12:52.838
so I had to remove it after a few minutes.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:54.740
It recommends that you
leave it on for five,

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:57.143
but I couldn't take it anymore. I'm sorry.

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:59.011
I did see a slight brightening effect,

00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:00.679
but it wasn't blowing me away.

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:02.248
I could still see my dark circles

00:13:02.248 --> 00:13:04.049
peeking through a bit. I do, however,

00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:06.218
think that this is a nice powder formula.

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:08.788
It's really smoothing
and super-finely milled,

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:10.489
but they need to get rid of the scent.

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:13.058
Maybelline just dropped
its Super Stay Vinyl Ink

00:13:13.058 --> 00:13:15.194
Longwear No-Budge Liquid Lipcolor.

00:13:15.194 --> 00:13:16.695
This is a long-wearing lipstick

00:13:16.695 --> 00:13:18.030
that's meant to stay shiny,

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.698
which really got my attention.

00:13:19.698 --> 00:13:22.668
You have to shake it for
five seconds, then apply.

00:13:22.668 --> 00:13:24.136
When I first started applying,

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:26.539
I got nervous because
it looked really patchy,

00:13:26.539 --> 00:13:29.008
but I got full coverage
when I added another layer,

00:13:29.008 --> 00:13:31.777
and it surprisingly felt
lightweight on the lips.

00:13:31.777 --> 00:13:33.479
I kissed my hand to check for transfer,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.114
and there definitely was some.

00:13:35.114 --> 00:13:36.682
I did a test wearing my mask

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:38.317
and saw some transfer there too.

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:39.685
And then I took a sip of my drink

00:13:39.685 --> 00:13:41.954
and saw minimal transfer there as well.

00:13:41.954 --> 00:13:43.756
Even though I was
getting a little transfer

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:45.491
and most of the shine was gone,

00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.827
the lipstick itself
still looked super bright

00:13:47.827 --> 00:13:50.396
and it didn't move anywhere,
so I was happy with that.

00:13:50.396 --> 00:13:53.365
This is the Dior Backstage
Flash Perfector concealer.

00:13:53.365 --> 00:13:55.401
I think the main thing
that's special about this

00:13:55.401 --> 00:13:57.136
is that it has a brush applicator

00:13:57.136 --> 00:13:58.704
instead of a doe-foot applicator,

00:13:58.704 --> 00:14:01.340
so that's supposed to
be easier to blend in.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.309
I still had to use my sponge for blending,

00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:06.045
but I did like how easy
application was with the brush,

00:14:06.045 --> 00:14:07.947
although I wouldn't say it was any easier

00:14:07.947 --> 00:14:10.115
than a regular doe-foot applicator.

00:14:10.115 --> 00:14:12.051
The formula itself is really nice.

00:14:12.051 --> 00:14:13.752
The coverage is more on the medium side,

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:15.120
but it covered enough.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.322
I like this concealer,

00:14:16.322 --> 00:14:18.290
but I wouldn't tell you
to go run and get it.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.627
It's just a nice concealer
with a high-end name on it.

00:14:21.627 --> 00:14:23.696
The Beauty Blender Power Pocket Puff

00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:26.265
is basically a double-sided velour puff.

00:14:26.265 --> 00:14:28.601
So the pink side is
for powder application,

00:14:28.601 --> 00:14:31.637
and the tan side is for
blending the powder and makeup.

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:33.239
It does pick up a lot of product.

00:14:33.239 --> 00:14:35.074
I tried to tap off as much as I could,

00:14:35.074 --> 00:14:37.810
but it still deposited a lot of powder.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.612
It is described as a tool you can use

00:14:39.612 --> 00:14:41.180
for baking the under-eye area,

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.448
so maybe that's why.

00:14:42.448 --> 00:14:44.183
The shape does make it easy to use,

00:14:44.183 --> 00:14:46.118
and I liked how it has
this little strap on it

00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:47.920
that can be used on either side.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.488
After leaving the powder on for a bit,

00:14:49.488 --> 00:14:51.190
I used the tan side to blend it in,

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.925
and it wasn't getting
rid of all the powder,

00:14:52.925 --> 00:14:55.494
so I did use a brush
to dust off the excess.

00:14:55.494 --> 00:14:56.929
I noticed that my under-eye area

00:14:56.929 --> 00:14:58.864
looked really smooth, smoother than when

00:14:58.864 --> 00:15:00.966
I set the area with my normal sponge.

00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:03.502
The lines under my eyes
weren't as defined.

00:15:03.502 --> 00:15:05.804
This is the new MAC MACStack mascara,

00:15:05.804 --> 00:15:07.706
and it's supposed to be super volumizing,

00:15:07.706 --> 00:15:09.675
which I love. What I don't love

00:15:09.675 --> 00:15:12.578
is a plastic mascara
brush, which this has,

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.713
but I was still excited to try this.

00:15:14.713 --> 00:15:16.115
When I first started applying,

00:15:16.115 --> 00:15:19.218
I immediately hated the
feeling of the brush on my eye.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:21.220
It's a little too spiky
for someone like me

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.755
with pretty sensitive eyes.

00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:25.658
I noticed an instant lift
and volume with my lashes,

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:27.693
which are naturally pretty straight.

00:15:27.693 --> 00:15:29.061
I did another coat and loved

00:15:29.061 --> 00:15:30.296
how this made my lashes look.

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:33.198
They look long and full
without looking clumpy.

00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:35.868
I don't know if I can
justify $28 for mascara,

00:15:35.868 --> 00:15:37.236
but this one is so good.

00:15:37.236 --> 00:15:39.438
I might have to splurge
on it every now and then.

00:15:39.438 --> 00:15:41.740
We have two new face products
from One/Size Beauty,

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:43.909
the Cheek Clapper 3D blush trio palette

00:15:43.909 --> 00:15:46.245
and the Made for Shade
bronze and sculpt trio.

00:15:46.245 --> 00:15:48.480
Let's get into the sculpt palette first.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.215
I used a mix of the bottom two shades,

00:15:50.215 --> 00:15:52.885
and they brought some
much-needed warmth for my face.

00:15:52.885 --> 00:15:54.954
They blend really nicely and smoothly.

00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:56.155
These are nice bronzers,

00:15:56.155 --> 00:15:58.223
but I think the real star of the show here

00:15:58.223 --> 00:15:59.825
is the blush palette.

00:15:59.825 --> 00:16:01.727
If I had to pick one of these two palettes

00:16:01.727 --> 00:16:04.396
to splurge on, it would
definitely be this one.

00:16:04.396 --> 00:16:05.764
These are three different formulas,

00:16:05.764 --> 00:16:07.800
a flex cream, a full-impact
matte,

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.301
and a hyper sheen.

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:10.669
I went in with a very light hand

00:16:10.669 --> 00:16:12.271
because these are really pigmented,

00:16:12.271 --> 00:16:13.939
and they just look really beautiful

00:16:13.939 --> 00:16:15.841
and smooth on the skin.

00:16:15.841 --> 00:16:17.776
The color can be built up or toned down

00:16:17.776 --> 00:16:18.610
as much as you want,

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.113
which I think is my favorite
thing about this palette.

00:16:21.113 --> 00:16:23.248
There are just so many
different ways you can use it,

00:16:23.248 --> 00:16:25.584
and all the formulas
work so nicely together.

00:16:25.584 --> 00:16:26.685
Rare Beauty just released the

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:29.421
Positive Light tinted
moisturizer with SPF 20.

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:31.991
I was so happy that this had SPF in it.

00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:33.425
The formula felt thicker

00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:35.928
and looked more full-coverage
than I expected.

00:16:35.928 --> 00:16:38.297
Also, this was a shade
or two too light for me,

00:16:38.297 --> 00:16:39.498
so ignore that.

00:16:39.498 --> 00:16:41.300
It does sheer out as you apply it,

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.835
so it looks less like a foundation

00:16:42.835 --> 00:16:44.937
and more like a tinted moisturizer.

00:16:44.937 --> 00:16:47.106
I applied the rest of
my powder makeup on top

00:16:47.106 --> 00:16:49.508
and honestly wasn't loving how it looked.

00:16:49.508 --> 00:16:50.843
I felt like it kept building up

00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:52.378
in the dry patches around my nose

00:16:52.378 --> 00:16:55.280
and just looked a little too textured.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.449
But then I redid my makeup
with all cream products

00:16:57.449 --> 00:16:59.118
on top of this tinted moisturizer,

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.652
and it looked so much better,

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:02.221
just super dewy and fresh.

00:17:02.221 --> 00:17:04.890
So I much preferred using
it with cream products.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.359
This is the NYX Wonder
Stick cream blush contour,

00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:08.861
and it's literally a blush stick

00:17:08.861 --> 00:17:10.996
that you use to contour your face.

00:17:10.996 --> 00:17:11.830
There's a lighter shade

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.198
that's meant to be used as a blush

00:17:13.198 --> 00:17:15.401
and a deeper shade that you contour with.

00:17:15.401 --> 00:17:17.069
I have never contoured with blush,

00:17:17.069 --> 00:17:18.837
so I was really intrigued by this.

00:17:18.837 --> 00:17:20.072
I applied the darker shade

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:21.673
wherever I would normally contour

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:22.975
and the lighter shade above it

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:24.710
and then blended it out.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:26.812
This isn't the easiest formula to blend,

00:17:26.812 --> 00:17:28.814
but I eventually got
it looking pretty good.

00:17:28.814 --> 00:17:30.816
I didn't hate the blush-contour look.

00:17:30.816 --> 00:17:32.718
I just think this blush
formula isn't great,

00:17:32.718 --> 00:17:35.220
and I've definitely tried
better at the drugstore.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.256
I haven't experimented
much with correctors,

00:17:37.256 --> 00:17:39.491
but I saw a TikTok recommending this one,

00:17:39.491 --> 00:17:41.093
the Benefit Boi-ing Bright On

00:17:41.093 --> 00:17:43.162
brightening undereye concealer.

00:17:43.162 --> 00:17:44.430
It has this peachy color

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.032
to counteract the darkness
underneath the eyes.

00:17:47.032 --> 00:17:49.034
I tested it out before applying makeup,

00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:50.769
and I could see a difference already.

00:17:50.769 --> 00:17:53.405
So then I applied a small
amount, blended that,

00:17:53.405 --> 00:17:54.907
then applied concealer on top,

00:17:54.907 --> 00:17:56.508
and I think it did make a difference.

00:17:56.508 --> 00:17:58.777
My under-eyes looked brighter than usual.

00:17:58.777 --> 00:18:00.546
I definitely noticed less darkness

00:18:00.546 --> 00:18:02.014
than when I just use concealer,

00:18:02.014 --> 00:18:03.582
and the product didn't do anything weird

00:18:03.582 --> 00:18:05.717
to the concealer I applied on top.

00:18:05.717 --> 00:18:07.386
It didn't make it patchy or bunch up,

00:18:07.386 --> 00:18:08.887
so I'm actually really into this.

00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:10.856
I realized later you're just supposed

00:18:10.856 --> 00:18:11.890
to wear this on its own,

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.292
which I clearly did not do.

00:18:13.292 --> 00:18:15.394
But I was still happy with the results.

00:18:15.394 --> 00:18:16.595
Charlotte Tilbury came out

00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:18.030
with a new Pillow Talk collection

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.732
inspired by its popular
lipstick in Pillow Talk,

00:18:20.732 --> 00:18:22.534
so I picked up a few of the products.

00:18:22.534 --> 00:18:24.203
I already love the Beauty Light Wands,

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:26.472
so I knew that I would love
this Pillow Talk shade.

00:18:26.472 --> 00:18:29.641
It's super glowy and makes
the skin look so beautiful.

00:18:29.641 --> 00:18:31.944
The Multi-Glow highlighter
was a new product for me.

00:18:31.944 --> 00:18:33.946
The packaging is so pretty.

00:18:33.946 --> 00:18:36.215
I didn't even want to touch it, but I did.

00:18:36.215 --> 00:18:38.050
It has this almost soft blurring effect

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.251
that looks really nice.

00:18:39.251 --> 00:18:40.953
And it's not glittery at all,

00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:42.488
just like a soft glow.

00:18:42.488 --> 00:18:44.289
The product I was most excited to try

00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:46.725
was actually the mascara
in the shade Dream Pop.

00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:49.128
It's described as a berry-brown shade.

00:18:49.128 --> 00:18:50.329
I don't think I have ever tried

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:51.563
a colored mascara before,

00:18:51.563 --> 00:18:53.232
but I applied it like I normally would,

00:18:53.232 --> 00:18:54.800
and I actually love the color.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.235
The formula isn't my favorite,

00:18:56.235 --> 00:18:58.003
and neither is the brush,
but I think the color

00:18:58.003 --> 00:18:59.905
was actually flattering on my eyes.

00:18:59.905 --> 00:19:02.608
It's supposed to bring out
the amber in brown eyes.

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:03.909
I don't know if that's what's happening,

00:19:03.909 --> 00:19:04.843
but it did make my eyes look

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:06.678
really sparkly, which I love.

00:19:06.678 --> 00:19:08.247
I saw that Flower Beauty had this

00:19:08.247 --> 00:19:09.581
Spotlight liquid highlighter

00:19:09.581 --> 00:19:11.483
that looked a lot like
the Charlotte Tilbury

00:19:11.483 --> 00:19:12.951
Light Wand in the Pillow Talk shade,

00:19:12.951 --> 00:19:14.520
so I really wanted to compare the two

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.754
to see if it was a dupe.

00:19:15.754 --> 00:19:17.289
The shades aren't exactly the same,

00:19:17.289 --> 00:19:18.590
but they're super close.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.259
Both are so easy to blend out

00:19:20.259 --> 00:19:22.161
and look more natural and dewy on the skin

00:19:22.161 --> 00:19:23.829
than a powder highlight does.

00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:25.130
I think the Charlotte Tilbury one

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.266
is a bit more reflective
than the Flower Beauty one,

00:19:27.266 --> 00:19:29.468
but the effect is definitely similar.

00:19:29.468 --> 00:19:32.004
The Flower Beauty one looks
just as beautiful on the skin,

00:19:32.004 --> 00:19:33.839
and it's almost $30 cheaper.

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:35.707
So I highly recommend this if you haven't

00:19:35.707 --> 00:19:37.676
gotten the chance to try the Light Wands.

00:19:37.676 --> 00:19:39.011
I'm an East Coast girl,

00:19:39.011 --> 00:19:40.846
so I was so excited when I saw

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:42.347
that ELF collabed with Dunkin'.

00:19:42.347 --> 00:19:44.683
This was such a fun, cute idea.

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:46.885
This huge doughnut
sponge was so ridiculous,

00:19:46.885 --> 00:19:48.287
I had to try it out.

00:19:48.287 --> 00:19:49.988
It's big even before wetting,

00:19:49.988 --> 00:19:51.456
and it was pretty hard at first.

00:19:51.456 --> 00:19:53.225
But it doubled in size once I wet it,

00:19:53.225 --> 00:19:56.028
and it became a lot softer and squishier.

00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:57.062
I'm not gonna lie,

00:19:57.062 --> 00:19:59.531
applying foundation with
this is kind of great

00:19:59.531 --> 00:20:00.832
because it's so big.

00:20:00.832 --> 00:20:04.036
It literally applies
foundation in five seconds.

00:20:04.036 --> 00:20:06.305
I decided to use it to
apply all my other makeup,

00:20:06.305 --> 00:20:08.640
and the size does get more
difficult to work with

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.242
the more precise you're trying to be.

00:20:10.242 --> 00:20:11.577
You can see that I was accidentally

00:20:11.577 --> 00:20:13.345
spreading my blush up way too high.

00:20:13.345 --> 00:20:16.048
But I think overall, the
makeup came out looking good.

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:18.317
Obviously, this is more like a novelty

00:20:18.317 --> 00:20:20.018
than a super-useful makeup tool,

00:20:20.018 --> 00:20:22.888
but it comes in handy if you
want to apply makeup quickly.

00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:25.057
I also ordered the Glazed
for Days lip gloss set

00:20:25.057 --> 00:20:27.326
because I cannot resist an orange gloss,

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:28.527
let alone an orange gloss

00:20:28.527 --> 00:20:30.362
that smells like glazed doughnuts.

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:31.930
This is a really nice gloss.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.098
The color is pretty sheer,

00:20:33.098 --> 00:20:33.999
but for the price point,

00:20:33.999 --> 00:20:35.767
I think this formula is super glossy

00:20:35.767 --> 00:20:37.636
and comfortable on the lips.

00:20:37.636 --> 00:20:39.871
Donni Davy, the head makeup
artist of "Euphoria,"

00:20:39.871 --> 00:20:42.074
just came out with her own
makeup line, Half Magic,

00:20:42.074 --> 00:20:44.710
and I bought a bunch of
products to test out.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.145
First up, we have these
Chromaddiction matte eye paints.

00:20:47.145 --> 00:20:48.347
They have a lot of pigment

00:20:48.347 --> 00:20:50.415
and were really easy to layer and blend.

00:20:50.415 --> 00:20:51.650
They don't dry down too fast,

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.918
and you can use them as eyeliner,

00:20:52.918 --> 00:20:54.086
which is what I did.

00:20:54.086 --> 00:20:56.455
They have this reusable
wing guide, which was OK.

00:20:56.455 --> 00:20:58.423
I feel like it was a little too flimsy,

00:20:58.423 --> 00:21:00.926
so I didn't get that
great of a wing with this.

00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:03.128
This Glitterpill was so pretty,

00:21:03.128 --> 00:21:05.530
and the applicator made it so easy to use.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.266
Plus, you don't have
to use a glitter base.

00:21:07.266 --> 00:21:09.434
It just dries down and stays put.

00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:10.736
The Light Trap glow powders

00:21:10.736 --> 00:21:12.638
definitely do give you a nice glow,

00:21:12.638 --> 00:21:14.539
and you can use them anywhere on the face.

00:21:14.539 --> 00:21:16.275
Like, I put this purple one on my eyes,

00:21:16.275 --> 00:21:18.443
and it looked so cool.

00:21:18.443 --> 00:21:20.379
Of course, I also had
to get these iridescent

00:21:20.379 --> 00:21:22.014
face gems, which are self-adhering,

00:21:22.014 --> 00:21:24.049
so you don't need any
glue for the first use.

00:21:24.049 --> 00:21:26.518
You will need glue if you reuse them.

00:21:26.518 --> 00:21:30.122
These are so easy to apply
and add such a cute sparkle.

00:21:30.122 --> 00:21:32.924
The last product I got was
the Magic Brownie Liptrik Kit.

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:35.127
It has a darker and lighter lip liner,

00:21:35.127 --> 00:21:37.062
so you can customize the lipstick.

00:21:37.062 --> 00:21:39.598
The lip liner is very smooth and creamy,

00:21:39.598 --> 00:21:42.501
and this lipstick is super
comfortable on the lips.

00:21:42.501 --> 00:21:44.436
This brand as a whole really inspires you

00:21:44.436 --> 00:21:46.238
to play with your makeup, which I love,

00:21:46.238 --> 00:21:48.473
and I really liked the
products that I tried.

00:21:48.473 --> 00:21:50.776
I'm excited to see what
they come out with next.

00:21:50.776 --> 00:21:52.544
Danessa Myricks Beauty just released

00:21:52.544 --> 00:21:54.713
this Skin Blurring Balm Powder.

00:21:54.713 --> 00:21:57.049
I got the universal shade,
which is translucent,

00:21:57.049 --> 00:21:58.984
and I also got the shade 4.

00:21:58.984 --> 00:22:00.952
So, you can use this as a primer,

00:22:00.952 --> 00:22:03.488
concealer and contour, a foundation,

00:22:03.488 --> 00:22:06.224
or it can be used to set your foundation.

00:22:06.224 --> 00:22:08.694
I first tried the
universal one as a primer

00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:10.429
under my go-to foundation.

00:22:10.429 --> 00:22:12.831
The texture is kind of strange.

00:22:12.831 --> 00:22:15.667
It blends in easily like a balm would,

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:19.871
but it dries down to, like,
a soft-matte powder finish.

00:22:19.871 --> 00:22:22.007
It really does blur a
lot of imperfections.

00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:24.409
My foundation went over this so smoothly,

00:22:24.409 --> 00:22:26.244
and it did make it slightly more matte

00:22:26.244 --> 00:22:28.547
than it usually looks, but I didn't mind.

00:22:28.547 --> 00:22:31.183
Then I tried the tinted
shade just as a foundation.

00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:33.151
It did take me a while to blend out,

00:22:33.151 --> 00:22:35.721
but once I did, I really liked the finish.

00:22:35.721 --> 00:22:38.523
This is actually more full
coverage than I was expecting.

00:22:38.523 --> 00:22:40.559
I feel like it covered a lot!

00:22:40.559 --> 00:22:42.661
I did end up wearing
this for the entire day,

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:44.996
and I noticed that I was much less oily

00:22:44.996 --> 00:22:47.065
at the end of the day than usual.

00:22:47.065 --> 00:22:48.734
It does have a bit of a learning curve,

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:50.369
but once you figure out
how to make this work

00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:52.938
for your skin, it's a really cool product.

00:22:52.938 --> 00:22:54.873
I don't know why it's taken me this long

00:22:54.873 --> 00:22:57.242
to try the About-Face
Matte Fluid Eye Paints,

00:22:57.242 --> 00:22:58.777
but I'm finally doing it.

00:22:58.777 --> 00:23:01.246
These are liquid eye colors that come in

00:23:01.246 --> 00:23:04.015
full-coverage mattes or sheer shades.

00:23:04.015 --> 00:23:05.817
Don't be scared by that orange swatch.

00:23:05.817 --> 00:23:07.185
That one is a sheer shade.

00:23:07.185 --> 00:23:09.321
The pigment in these is incredible.

00:23:09.321 --> 00:23:12.124
They're super easy to
apply and to blend out.

00:23:12.124 --> 00:23:13.725
You can build up the color if you want,

00:23:13.725 --> 00:23:15.560
and it still feels lightweight.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:17.362
Plus, I'm in love with this packaging.

00:23:17.362 --> 00:23:19.731
These are amazing, and I need more colors.

00:23:19.731 --> 00:23:22.200
The Espressoh Glassy blush is one of those

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.935
pH-reactive products.

00:23:23.935 --> 00:23:27.272
It goes from clear to a
pink tint on the skin.

00:23:27.272 --> 00:23:29.274
I first tried it over my foundation,

00:23:29.274 --> 00:23:30.509
and it started to break down

00:23:30.509 --> 00:23:32.377
the product I already had on.

00:23:32.377 --> 00:23:35.080
It was pilling so much.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:36.848
So we were off to a bad start.

00:23:36.848 --> 00:23:38.717
I tried it out on my bare skin,

00:23:38.717 --> 00:23:40.218
and it worked a lot better.

00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:42.320
It's cute and a fun idea,

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:43.688
but I'm not blown away by this.

00:23:43.688 --> 00:23:45.056
I would rather just get a blush

00:23:45.056 --> 00:23:47.559
that works on skin and over makeup.

00:23:47.559 --> 00:23:50.395
This is the Bdellium large
rounded double dome blender,

00:23:50.395 --> 00:23:52.431
and it looks like a little mouth.

00:23:52.431 --> 00:23:54.966
It's basically like two brushes in one.

00:23:54.966 --> 00:23:57.135
It's supposed to blend
in product really fast

00:23:57.135 --> 00:23:59.037
and give you an airbrushed finish.

00:23:59.037 --> 00:24:00.605
You can use it with any liquid,

00:24:00.605 --> 00:24:02.073
cream, or powder product,

00:24:02.073 --> 00:24:04.142
so I decided I would do a full face

00:24:04.142 --> 00:24:05.377
with just this brush.

00:24:05.377 --> 00:24:08.113
I was immediately blown
away by how quickly

00:24:08.113 --> 00:24:10.215
and seamlessly this
blended in the product.

00:24:10.215 --> 00:24:13.685
Plus, this was, like, the
softest brush I've ever felt.

00:24:13.685 --> 00:24:15.754
You're supposed to do these
back-and-forth motions,

00:24:15.754 --> 00:24:17.456
and I thought it would look so streaky,

00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:20.625
but it just looked really
smooth and well blended.

00:24:20.625 --> 00:24:23.228
Because of the size, it is
a little difficult to use

00:24:23.228 --> 00:24:25.430
for the more precise
products, like concealer,

00:24:25.430 --> 00:24:27.732
but they do sell smaller
sizes of this brush.

00:24:27.732 --> 00:24:29.134
I loved it.

00:24:29.134 --> 00:24:31.102
This is the Saie Hydrabeam brightening

00:24:31.102 --> 00:24:32.871
and hydrating under-eye concealer.

00:24:32.871 --> 00:24:35.674
It has a radiant finish,
which had me a little worried.

00:24:35.674 --> 00:24:37.075
I don't really think "radiant"

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:38.677
when I'm picking out a concealer.

00:24:38.677 --> 00:24:41.980
The coverage is light, a
little too light for my taste.

00:24:41.980 --> 00:24:43.615
I'm a medium- to full-coverage girl

00:24:43.615 --> 00:24:44.716
when it comes to concealer,

00:24:44.716 --> 00:24:47.319
but the finish is pretty and skin-like.

00:24:47.319 --> 00:24:49.955
It also looked good when
I set it with powder,

00:24:49.955 --> 00:24:52.924
but I absolutely hate
the applicator on this.

00:24:52.924 --> 00:24:55.060
In my opinion, it's too short.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:57.462
It is so stiff, and it
doesn't do a great job

00:24:57.462 --> 00:24:59.998
of picking up and spreading
the product around.

00:24:59.998 --> 00:25:03.768
Other than that, this is a
very nice everyday concealer.

00:25:03.768 --> 00:25:06.171
These are the Tarte
Maracuja Juicy Lip Plumps,

00:25:06.171 --> 00:25:09.241
and they're supposed to give
you a tingle-free plumping.

00:25:09.241 --> 00:25:11.309
They actually are so juicy.

00:25:11.309 --> 00:25:12.878
Look at how shiny that is.

00:25:12.878 --> 00:25:14.613
My first reaction to these was that

00:25:14.613 --> 00:25:16.448
they are incredibly fragile.

00:25:16.448 --> 00:25:17.849
Like, you want to be careful with how much

00:25:17.849 --> 00:25:19.985
pressure you're using,
because it will break.

00:25:19.985 --> 00:25:21.353
So I didn't love that.

00:25:21.353 --> 00:25:23.788
But these feel so good on the lips.

00:25:23.788 --> 00:25:25.924
Like, I could not stop
rubbing them together.

00:25:25.924 --> 00:25:28.326
It's so comfortable and hydrating.

00:25:28.326 --> 00:25:31.129
The plumping was actually
tingle-free for me.

00:25:31.129 --> 00:25:34.633
It just felt minty, like I
rubbed toothpaste on my lips.

00:25:34.633 --> 00:25:35.934
The plumping effect is subtle,

00:25:35.934 --> 00:25:38.203
but I still really liked these.

00:25:38.203 --> 00:25:39.070
I did it.

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:41.806
I bought the Jones Road
Beauty What the Foundation.

00:25:41.806 --> 00:25:44.809
This has caused all kinds of
controversy and discourse,

00:25:44.809 --> 00:25:47.979
so I apologize for also
putting in my 2 cents.

00:25:47.979 --> 00:25:49.214
This is what it looks like.

00:25:49.214 --> 00:25:51.950
It's very oily and thick.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:54.152
It has a scent I actually don't mind.

00:25:54.152 --> 00:25:56.788
It's like a soft, spa-like smell.

00:25:56.788 --> 00:25:59.791
I applied a pretty small
amount for me with my fingers

00:25:59.791 --> 00:26:01.893
and then went over that with my sponge,

00:26:01.893 --> 00:26:05.463
and I did not hate how this looked.

00:26:05.463 --> 00:26:06.831
It's very skin-like.

00:26:06.831 --> 00:26:09.434
It felt like I wasn't
even wearing foundation.

00:26:09.434 --> 00:26:12.437
I will say it tends to
gather in certain areas,

00:26:12.437 --> 00:26:15.473
so I might have to go in
with even less product.

00:26:15.473 --> 00:26:17.609
My other products layered
on top of this fine,

00:26:17.609 --> 00:26:19.010
but I feel like I like this more

00:26:19.010 --> 00:26:20.412
as an everyday skin tint

00:26:20.412 --> 00:26:22.948
rather than a foundation
base for my makeup.

00:26:22.948 --> 00:26:24.082
Like, I would reach for this

00:26:24.082 --> 00:26:26.084
when I'm running errands
on a Sunday morning,

00:26:26.084 --> 00:26:27.919
but not when I'm going to the club.

00:26:27.919 --> 00:26:29.821
I've been obsessed with lip oil,

00:26:29.821 --> 00:26:31.323
so I immediately snapped up

00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:32.958
this Fenty Beauty Cherry Treat

00:26:32.958 --> 00:26:35.427
conditioning and strengthening lip oil.

00:26:35.427 --> 00:26:36.962
I have to start off by saying

00:26:36.962 --> 00:26:39.598
this is the most
amazing-smelling lip product.

00:26:39.598 --> 00:26:42.167
It smells like cherry candies.

00:26:42.167 --> 00:26:44.769
We got this giant doe-foot
applicator I love.

00:26:44.769 --> 00:26:46.504
I did not want to stop applying this.

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:47.973
It felt so nice.

00:26:47.973 --> 00:26:49.441
This formula makes your lips feel

00:26:49.441 --> 00:26:51.876
so hydrated and soft and cushiony,

00:26:51.876 --> 00:26:53.545
if that makes any sense.

00:26:53.545 --> 00:26:55.480
It's also so glossy.

00:26:55.480 --> 00:26:56.815
The color is so sheer

00:26:56.815 --> 00:26:58.950
it doesn't really look
like much on my lips,

00:26:58.950 --> 00:26:59.818
but I love this,

00:26:59.818 --> 00:27:01.886
and it's definitely going in my bag.

00:27:01.886 --> 00:27:03.288
I also got the Fenty Beauty

00:27:03.288 --> 00:27:05.190
Poutsicle hydrating lip stain.

00:27:05.190 --> 00:27:07.459
This also feels so good on the lips.

00:27:07.459 --> 00:27:08.660
Every lip stain I've tried

00:27:08.660 --> 00:27:11.029
has been more drying, not hydrating,

00:27:11.029 --> 00:27:13.131
so I am really into this formula.

00:27:13.131 --> 00:27:14.366
It's very pigmented,

00:27:14.366 --> 00:27:16.034
so I was careful when I was applying

00:27:16.034 --> 00:27:18.036
to make sure I didn't
get the stain anywhere

00:27:18.036 --> 00:27:19.571
outside of my lips.

00:27:19.571 --> 00:27:21.339
After leaving it on for a few minutes,

00:27:21.339 --> 00:27:23.141
I wiped it off with a paper towel,

00:27:23.141 --> 00:27:25.677
and there was definitely
a pretty stain left behind

00:27:25.677 --> 00:27:28.079
that was 100% transfer-proof.

00:27:28.079 --> 00:27:30.715
I can see myself wearing
this a lot this summer.

00:27:30.715 --> 00:27:31.750
If you can believe it,

00:27:31.750 --> 00:27:35.220
I have never tried a
Haus Labs product before.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:36.688
They recently rebranded,

00:27:36.688 --> 00:27:38.657
and I picked up a couple of products.

00:27:38.657 --> 00:27:42.060
First up, this Haus Labs
Hy-Power pigment paint.

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:44.229
You can use this anywhere on the face.

00:27:44.229 --> 00:27:46.598
The pigment in these
actually took me by surprise.

00:27:46.598 --> 00:27:49.934
Like, I was not expecting
them to be so full-coverage.

00:27:49.934 --> 00:27:52.337
You need the tiniest amount of these.

00:27:52.337 --> 00:27:54.339
It blended out pretty easily on my eyes,

00:27:54.339 --> 00:27:55.840
and it doesn't dry too quickly,

00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:57.442
so you have some time to work.

00:27:57.442 --> 00:27:59.344
I am so into these.

00:27:59.344 --> 00:28:02.180
I also picked up the PhD hybrid lip oil.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:05.016
This applicator is much
smaller than the Fenty one,

00:28:05.016 --> 00:28:06.217
which made me sad,

00:28:06.217 --> 00:28:08.353
but the actual formula is really smooth

00:28:08.353 --> 00:28:09.954
and comfortable on the lips.

00:28:09.954 --> 00:28:11.556
It's more of a thinner formula

00:28:11.556 --> 00:28:13.058
than other lip oils I've tried,

00:28:13.058 --> 00:28:15.727
but I really loved how
this looked and felt.

00:28:15.727 --> 00:28:17.095
This also has no scent,

00:28:17.095 --> 00:28:20.298
which I prefer over a bad scent.

00:28:20.298 --> 00:28:21.599
These were great products,

00:28:21.599 --> 00:28:23.201
and I need to try more.

00:28:23.201 --> 00:28:25.403
Uoma Beauty just released
this Trippin smooth powder,

00:28:25.403 --> 00:28:26.905
and what's so cool about it

00:28:26.905 --> 00:28:28.707
is how the powder dispenses.

00:28:28.707 --> 00:28:29.607
You twist it,

00:28:29.607 --> 00:28:31.710
and it releases the
perfect amount of powder,

00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:35.113
which I love because my
powders get so messy.

00:28:35.113 --> 00:28:38.450
The powder itself is so finely
milled and silky smooth.

00:28:38.450 --> 00:28:39.884
It applied really nicely

00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:41.386
and smoothed out my under-eyes a bit,

00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:42.821
so I really liked it.

00:28:42.821 --> 00:28:45.323
I've been on the hunt for
a good talc-free powder,

00:28:45.323 --> 00:28:46.758
and I think this is it.

00:28:46.758 --> 00:28:48.727
The only thing I wish they had

00:28:48.727 --> 00:28:50.161
was a translucent option,

00:28:50.161 --> 00:28:51.463
but this is so good.

00:28:51.463 --> 00:28:53.832
I tried two products
from Makeup Revolution.

00:28:53.832 --> 00:28:56.835
Let's start with this
Blush Bomb cream blusher.

00:28:56.835 --> 00:28:59.938
This straight up looks and
feels like a lip gloss.

00:28:59.938 --> 00:29:01.406
It was very confusing.

00:29:01.406 --> 00:29:03.775
It's definitely more of
an oily blush formula

00:29:03.775 --> 00:29:04.943
than I'm used to.

00:29:04.943 --> 00:29:06.644
First application wasn't great.

00:29:06.644 --> 00:29:08.813
It's pretty sheer, but it does build up.

00:29:08.813 --> 00:29:10.482
I don't think I like this, though.

00:29:10.482 --> 00:29:13.251
I think it just feels like
lip gloss on my cheeks.

00:29:13.251 --> 00:29:15.787
I also tried the Superfix misting spray.

00:29:15.787 --> 00:29:16.921
I know I just complained

00:29:16.921 --> 00:29:18.757
about the blush looking like a lip gloss,

00:29:18.757 --> 00:29:21.292
but I love that this
looks like a hair spray.

00:29:21.292 --> 00:29:22.127
The mist is nice,

00:29:22.127 --> 00:29:24.095
but I wish it was a continuous mist.

00:29:24.095 --> 00:29:25.830
I applied this underneath my makeup

00:29:25.830 --> 00:29:27.632
and then on top when I was finished.

00:29:27.632 --> 00:29:29.801
That's how I like to use setting spray.

00:29:29.801 --> 00:29:31.336
It melted the makeup in nicely,

00:29:31.336 --> 00:29:33.271
but I typically like a more dewy finish,

00:29:33.271 --> 00:29:34.672
and this is pretty matte.

00:29:34.672 --> 00:29:36.040
I wore this makeup for eight hours,

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:38.176
and I think I looked OK
at the end of the day.

00:29:38.176 --> 00:29:39.944
I feel like I could still see my blush,

00:29:39.944 --> 00:29:42.347
which is usually the
first thing to disappear.

00:29:42.347 --> 00:29:44.115
This isn't my favorite setting spray,

00:29:44.115 --> 00:29:46.785
but I do think it's a good cheaper option.

00:29:46.785 --> 00:29:48.186
Pat McGrath released a new shade

00:29:48.186 --> 00:29:51.022
of her Skin Fetish
highlighter and balm duo.

00:29:51.022 --> 00:29:52.690
This has a balm on one side

00:29:52.690 --> 00:29:55.193
and this really beautiful
highlighter on the other.

00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:58.229
This shade, Xtreme Cyber
Orchid, is so interesting.

00:29:58.229 --> 00:30:00.498
It shifts from a blue to a lilac

00:30:00.498 --> 00:30:03.201
and totally disappears at certain angles.

00:30:03.201 --> 00:30:05.069
This formula is definitely balmy,

00:30:05.069 --> 00:30:06.538
but not in an oily way.

00:30:06.538 --> 00:30:09.073
I got so nervous when I first applied it,

00:30:09.073 --> 00:30:11.576
because this was not blending in at all,

00:30:11.576 --> 00:30:12.911
but it blended in really nicely

00:30:12.911 --> 00:30:14.546
when I used my fingers.

00:30:14.546 --> 00:30:16.381
I think for 58 bucks I would rather get

00:30:16.381 --> 00:30:18.016
a more wearable everyday shade,

00:30:18.016 --> 00:30:20.151
but this formula is really nice.

00:30:20.151 --> 00:30:22.921
This is the Maybelline Tattoo
Studio brow-lift stick,

00:30:22.921 --> 00:30:24.589
which is supposed to give you a brow lift

00:30:24.589 --> 00:30:27.058
or a brow-lamination effect at home.

00:30:27.058 --> 00:30:28.860
It has a cool little brush on one side

00:30:28.860 --> 00:30:31.062
and then this colored wax on the other.

00:30:31.062 --> 00:30:33.064
So you brush your brows up first,

00:30:33.064 --> 00:30:34.399
apply the wax to fill in,

00:30:34.399 --> 00:30:37.202
and then use the brush
to lift the brow hairs.

00:30:37.202 --> 00:30:38.570
This is a cool idea,

00:30:38.570 --> 00:30:40.572
and I did like how it made my brows look,

00:30:40.572 --> 00:30:42.407
but it did take a bit of work.

00:30:42.407 --> 00:30:44.542
I think if this brush had firmer bristles,

00:30:44.542 --> 00:30:47.278
it would be easier to get
that brow-lift effect.

00:30:47.278 --> 00:30:49.614
I also just don't think
this wax is waxy enough

00:30:49.614 --> 00:30:52.917
to hold my brows up all
day, so this was just OK.

00:30:52.917 --> 00:30:55.620
I'm a big fan of the Made
by Mitchell Blurshes.

00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:57.522
I tried a purple blush from them before,

00:30:57.522 --> 00:30:59.157
and I loved it, and they just came out

00:30:59.157 --> 00:31:01.659
with a lavender shade, so I had to try it.

00:31:01.659 --> 00:31:04.495
Applying it on top of
my makeup was a mistake,

00:31:04.495 --> 00:31:06.197
because it's a pastel.

00:31:06.197 --> 00:31:08.633
It was basically like
I applied a white blush

00:31:08.633 --> 00:31:09.968
over my bronzer.

00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:12.003
Plus, it actually made
my foundation patchy,

00:31:12.003 --> 00:31:15.006
which is an issue that I've
never had with this formula.

00:31:15.006 --> 00:31:17.208
I think I might've just overblended.

00:31:17.208 --> 00:31:19.244
Trying it out on bare
skin wasn't any better.

00:31:19.244 --> 00:31:21.880
It just leaves this
very gray-looking cast.

00:31:21.880 --> 00:31:24.015
I looked like the Corpse Bride.

00:31:24.015 --> 00:31:25.350
I think I'm better off using this

00:31:25.350 --> 00:31:27.619
as an eyeliner and eye-shadow base.

00:31:27.619 --> 00:31:30.421
Clinique has finally come
out with a lip-gloss version

00:31:30.421 --> 00:31:32.724
of its iconic Black Honey lipstick.

00:31:32.724 --> 00:31:34.659
This color is definitely identical

00:31:34.659 --> 00:31:37.328
to the lipstick version, just glossy.

00:31:37.328 --> 00:31:39.030
Here's what they look like side by side.

00:31:39.030 --> 00:31:41.599
I liked it a little more
once I dabbed some off.

00:31:41.599 --> 00:31:43.835
This color is just really flattering.

00:31:43.835 --> 00:31:45.970
I have to say, though, this gloss formula

00:31:45.970 --> 00:31:47.705
is not my favorite.

00:31:47.705 --> 00:31:50.108
I think they were going
for a cushiony feel,

00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:52.610
but it's just kind of sticky and thick.

00:31:52.610 --> 00:31:55.146
Looks great, but it doesn't feel so great.

00:31:55.146 --> 00:31:57.882
ELF released this Halo Glow Liquid Filter,

00:31:57.882 --> 00:31:59.651
and the world stopped.

00:31:59.651 --> 00:32:01.085
Could this actually be a dupe

00:32:01.085 --> 00:32:03.988
for the Charlotte Tilbury
Flawless Filter? Let's see.

00:32:03.988 --> 00:32:06.457
On this side of my face I
applied Flawless Filter.

00:32:06.457 --> 00:32:08.893
It's gorgeous. It's glowy. It's perfect.

00:32:08.893 --> 00:32:11.763
Now, on this side, I
applied the ELF Halo Glow.

00:32:11.763 --> 00:32:13.364
Look at them side by side.

00:32:13.364 --> 00:32:15.066
They are almost identical.

00:32:15.066 --> 00:32:18.036
I would say that the ELF one
has a hint more coverage,

00:32:18.036 --> 00:32:19.270
but it still gives that same

00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:21.005
your-skin-but-better effect.

00:32:21.005 --> 00:32:24.108
And the Charlotte Tilbury
one is slightly more glowy.

00:32:24.108 --> 00:32:25.143
Slightly.

00:32:25.143 --> 00:32:27.245
I say save yourself the extra 30 bucks

00:32:27.245 --> 00:32:28.313
and get the ELF one.

00:32:28.313 --> 00:32:30.415
Side note: Look at the
size of this doe foot.

00:32:30.415 --> 00:32:31.449
It's huge!

00:32:31.449 --> 00:32:33.451
You guys know I adore Rare Beauty.

00:32:33.451 --> 00:32:35.153
I was so excited when they dropped

00:32:35.153 --> 00:32:38.122
these Kind Words matte
lipsticks and lip liners.

00:32:38.122 --> 00:32:39.490
I had to get the color Gifted,

00:32:39.490 --> 00:32:41.926
because Selena said that
that was her favorite.

00:32:41.926 --> 00:32:43.594
The lip liner is supersmooth.

00:32:43.594 --> 00:32:44.562
Even though it's matte,

00:32:44.562 --> 00:32:46.431
it doesn't drag or pull on the lips.

00:32:46.431 --> 00:32:48.232
Plus, it's a twist-up, which I love.

00:32:48.232 --> 00:32:50.435
The lipstick is so creamy and pigmented.

00:32:50.435 --> 00:32:52.737
You could probably put
this on in one swipe.

00:32:52.737 --> 00:32:54.605
It's definitely one of
the most comfortable

00:32:54.605 --> 00:32:56.374
matte lipsticks I've ever tried.

00:32:56.374 --> 00:32:58.609
Scrandie Beauty is a
brand I found on TikTok.

00:32:58.609 --> 00:33:01.846
I kept seeing videos of its
Spicy Sauce lip plumper,

00:33:01.846 --> 00:33:03.348
and I really wanted to test it out,

00:33:03.348 --> 00:33:05.616
since I haven't had much
luck with lip plumpers.

00:33:05.616 --> 00:33:06.918
I applied it to half my lips,

00:33:06.918 --> 00:33:09.087
so we could see if it
actually does anything.

00:33:09.087 --> 00:33:11.422
So, you apply it slightly
above your lip line,

00:33:11.422 --> 00:33:13.891
and it starts to feel a little spicy,

00:33:13.891 --> 00:33:16.361
then it starts to feel tingly and spicy,

00:33:16.361 --> 00:33:17.895
and then at the three-minute mark,

00:33:17.895 --> 00:33:20.865
you also start to feel
a warming sensation.

00:33:20.865 --> 00:33:22.400
I love lip plumpers,

00:33:22.400 --> 00:33:25.169
so I don't mind the roller
coaster this takes you on.

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:26.938
It feels kind of good to me.

00:33:26.938 --> 00:33:28.473
I definitely notice plumping,

00:33:28.473 --> 00:33:30.208
especially with my top lip.

00:33:30.208 --> 00:33:31.809
I really like this lip plumper,

00:33:31.809 --> 00:33:33.044
and I also like that it's clear,

00:33:33.044 --> 00:33:34.846
so you can wear it on top of anything.

00:33:34.846 --> 00:33:37.815
Eco Styler is the brand
of gel I use all the time,

00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:40.952
and I never knew it had
this Unicorn Glitter Gel.

00:33:40.952 --> 00:33:42.520
It's a translucent pink color

00:33:42.520 --> 00:33:44.455
with blue iridescent sparkles.

00:33:44.455 --> 00:33:45.656
It's so pretty.

00:33:45.656 --> 00:33:46.891
Running this through my hair,

00:33:46.891 --> 00:33:49.460
I feel like you don't really
get the glittery effect.

00:33:49.460 --> 00:33:52.363
It just kind of tinted my
hair this bluish color,

00:33:52.363 --> 00:33:53.297
which is cool,

00:33:53.297 --> 00:33:55.666
just not what I thought
it was going to look like.

00:33:55.666 --> 00:33:58.136
I definitely saw the
glitter and color better

00:33:58.136 --> 00:34:01.005
when I applied it to
brushed-back straight hair.

00:34:01.005 --> 00:34:03.241
I think this is cute for
a little glitter moment

00:34:03.241 --> 00:34:04.275
every once in a while.

00:34:04.275 --> 00:34:06.811
And it actually washed
out of my hair easily.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:07.912
I don't know if you guys know this,

00:34:07.912 --> 00:34:09.280
but I'm a nail-polish freak.

00:34:09.280 --> 00:34:12.116
So when I saw Dew by Jinsoon going viral,

00:34:12.116 --> 00:34:13.684
I bought it immediately.

00:34:13.684 --> 00:34:15.553
This is a milky-white polish.

00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:17.822
It's very sheer and soft.

00:34:17.822 --> 00:34:19.457
My nails are super stained right now,

00:34:19.457 --> 00:34:21.192
so I was worried about how it was looking

00:34:21.192 --> 00:34:22.593
after the first coat,

00:34:22.593 --> 00:34:24.262
but when I went in with that second coat,

00:34:24.262 --> 00:34:25.296
it looked really pretty,

00:34:25.296 --> 00:34:27.265
and my nails looked so much better.

00:34:27.265 --> 00:34:29.167
It was a little streaky in the first coat,

00:34:29.167 --> 00:34:31.369
but the second went on totally smooth.

00:34:31.369 --> 00:34:34.305
I do wish, though, that
this had a flat paddle brush

00:34:34.305 --> 00:34:37.408
instead of this brush just
to make it easier to paint.

00:34:37.408 --> 00:34:38.776
I'm sure you could find a really good

00:34:38.776 --> 00:34:40.144
drugstore dupe for this polish,

00:34:40.144 --> 00:34:41.746
because it is on the pricey side,

00:34:41.746 --> 00:34:43.081
but I really like it.

00:34:43.081 --> 00:34:45.583
This is the new Urban Decay Vice Lip Bond

00:34:45.583 --> 00:34:46.984
glossy liquid lipstick.

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:49.020
So you get the glossiness of a lip gloss

00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:50.755
and the wear of a liquid lipstick.

00:34:50.755 --> 00:34:52.490
This is extremely pigmented.

00:34:52.490 --> 00:34:53.991
I was really impressed by the color,

00:34:53.991 --> 00:34:55.726
but I feel like it wasn't as shiny

00:34:55.726 --> 00:34:57.128
as I thought it would be.

00:34:57.128 --> 00:34:58.696
I let it dry down for 10 minutes

00:34:58.696 --> 00:34:59.864
and kissed the back of my hand

00:34:59.864 --> 00:35:01.199
to see if it transferred at all,

00:35:01.199 --> 00:35:02.967
and it did, but only a little bit,

00:35:02.967 --> 00:35:04.735
and the lipstick still looked good.

00:35:04.735 --> 00:35:06.904
It's actually very
similar to the Maybelline

00:35:06.904 --> 00:35:09.073
Vinyl Ink lip color I tried a while ago,

00:35:09.073 --> 00:35:10.942
so I would probably recommend that one,

00:35:10.942 --> 00:35:13.344
since it's cheaper and performs the same.

00:35:13.344 --> 00:35:16.013
I am not a pot-concealer kind of person,

00:35:16.013 --> 00:35:17.682
but I was really excited to try out

00:35:17.682 --> 00:35:19.917
this REM Beauty Sweetener concealer.

00:35:19.917 --> 00:35:22.920
I also got the Dreamcloud
blender to test out as well.

00:35:22.920 --> 00:35:24.522
I scooped some up and just warmed it

00:35:24.522 --> 00:35:26.824
on the back of my hand.
Then I used my fingers

00:35:26.824 --> 00:35:29.293
to apply everywhere I wanted to conceal.

00:35:29.293 --> 00:35:31.762
The concealer looks thicker than it feels.

00:35:31.762 --> 00:35:34.165
I was actually surprised
at how lightweight it felt

00:35:34.165 --> 00:35:35.600
when I was blending it out.

00:35:35.600 --> 00:35:37.635
The coverage with this is amazing.

00:35:37.635 --> 00:35:40.004
I was so shocked at
how much it covered up.

00:35:40.004 --> 00:35:41.506
You don't need a lot at all.

00:35:41.506 --> 00:35:42.974
I definitely put too much on,

00:35:42.974 --> 00:35:44.709
but I really, really like this.

00:35:44.709 --> 00:35:46.444
They also included a black and white shade

00:35:46.444 --> 00:35:48.613
in this concealer, so you
can lighten your shade

00:35:48.613 --> 00:35:50.047
or deepen it, which is cool.

00:35:50.047 --> 00:35:51.716
I also really like this little sponge,

00:35:51.716 --> 00:35:53.718
but it's not worth $15.

00:35:53.718 --> 00:35:56.187
These NYX Ultimate Glow
Shots look so pretty

00:35:56.187 --> 00:35:57.889
that I literally bought three of them.

00:35:57.889 --> 00:35:59.557
They're supposed to be brightening

00:35:59.557 --> 00:36:01.492
and give a really glowy effect.

00:36:01.492 --> 00:36:03.194
Although these are gorgeous in the tube,

00:36:03.194 --> 00:36:05.730
they're just really
inconsistent on the eyes.

00:36:05.730 --> 00:36:08.099
The pigment on some is better than others,

00:36:08.099 --> 00:36:09.700
but overall, I would say the pigment

00:36:09.700 --> 00:36:11.235
isn't great with these on their own.

00:36:11.235 --> 00:36:12.537
I had to build them up a lot

00:36:12.537 --> 00:36:13.938
to get them to look like this.

00:36:13.938 --> 00:36:15.973
They definitely work better as a topper

00:36:15.973 --> 00:36:17.441
over other eye shadows.

00:36:17.441 --> 00:36:20.244
I'm so torn on these
because they look so good,

00:36:20.244 --> 00:36:22.947
but it takes a lot of
work to get them that way.

00:36:22.947 --> 00:36:25.383
I've been seeing these
gorgeous holo glosses

00:36:25.383 --> 00:36:27.618
from Queen Cosmetics all over TikTok.

00:36:27.618 --> 00:36:29.754
Of course, I had to get three of them.

00:36:29.754 --> 00:36:32.323
These glosses are just
as beautiful in person.

00:36:32.323 --> 00:36:34.091
They honestly feel fine on the lips,

00:36:34.091 --> 00:36:36.160
as long as you don't apply too much.

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:37.795
I packed on this Electric shade,

00:36:37.795 --> 00:36:39.730
and it did feel a little gritty,

00:36:39.730 --> 00:36:42.567
so I recommend only doing
one to two thin layers

00:36:42.567 --> 00:36:45.836
to avoid that, but these are so cool.

00:36:45.836 --> 00:36:46.938
They look good on their own

00:36:46.938 --> 00:36:48.739
but even better over lipstick,

00:36:48.739 --> 00:36:50.608
especially darker colors.

00:36:50.608 --> 00:36:53.144
This is the new Fenty Beauty Eaze Drop'Lit

00:36:53.144 --> 00:36:54.745
All-Over Glow Enhancer.

00:36:54.745 --> 00:36:57.648
It can be worn on its own
to reduce the look of pores

00:36:57.648 --> 00:37:00.484
or mixed into foundation
for some added glow.

00:37:00.484 --> 00:37:01.686
Using this on its own,

00:37:01.686 --> 00:37:03.821
I honestly wasn't very impressed.

00:37:03.821 --> 00:37:06.290
I don't think my pores
were necessarily blurred,

00:37:06.290 --> 00:37:09.160
and I felt like my skin
didn't look that glowy.

00:37:09.160 --> 00:37:12.029
It kind of just looked
like I applied moisturizer.

00:37:12.029 --> 00:37:14.665
I think this worked better
when mixed into a foundation.

00:37:14.665 --> 00:37:17.034
I mixed it with my Eaze
Drop Blurring Skin Tint,

00:37:17.034 --> 00:37:19.337
which I love, and I
noticed it gave my skin

00:37:19.337 --> 00:37:20.605
a nice little glow.

00:37:20.605 --> 00:37:22.673
This skin tint is more on the matte side,

00:37:22.673 --> 00:37:25.243
so I do like that the glow
enhancer made it more dewy.

00:37:25.243 --> 00:37:27.378
However, I don't think
it's such a big difference

00:37:27.378 --> 00:37:29.914
that I can justify buying this product.

00:37:29.914 --> 00:37:31.749
It kind of just feels like an extra step

00:37:31.749 --> 00:37:33.084
that doesn't add much.

00:37:33.084 --> 00:37:35.886
Item Beauty is Addison Rae's beauty brand.

00:37:35.886 --> 00:37:37.622
People rave about its lip oils,

00:37:37.622 --> 00:37:38.923
so I figured I'd test it out

00:37:38.923 --> 00:37:41.058
with a couple of other products too.

00:37:41.058 --> 00:37:43.694
So, this is the Lip Quip
moisturizing lip oil.

00:37:43.694 --> 00:37:46.631
Let me start out by
saying it smells amazing,

00:37:46.631 --> 00:37:47.965
kind of peachy.

00:37:47.965 --> 00:37:49.934
The color was actually
a little more pigmented

00:37:49.934 --> 00:37:51.469
than I expected for a lip oil,

00:37:51.469 --> 00:37:53.571
but I thought it was so pretty.

00:37:53.571 --> 00:37:55.473
The formula is on the thicker side.

00:37:55.473 --> 00:37:56.974
It feels super nourishing

00:37:56.974 --> 00:37:59.076
and just makes your lips look so juicy,

00:37:59.076 --> 00:38:00.978
so I am really into this.

00:38:00.978 --> 00:38:02.647
This is going in my bag.

00:38:02.647 --> 00:38:05.516
Next I tried the Boost
Juice dual-ended lash primer

00:38:05.516 --> 00:38:06.651
and colored mascara.

00:38:06.651 --> 00:38:09.654
So you can use this as a lash
primer or colored mascara.

00:38:09.654 --> 00:38:11.155
The lilac side is for volume,

00:38:11.155 --> 00:38:13.057
and the blue side is for lengthening.

00:38:13.057 --> 00:38:15.760
I have to admit I much
preferred the blue side

00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:17.695
as just a colored mascara.

00:38:17.695 --> 00:38:20.665
I feel like once I applied
regular mascara on top of it,

00:38:20.665 --> 00:38:23.034
my lashes just kind of lumped together.

00:38:23.034 --> 00:38:25.369
The lilac side barely
showed up on my lashes,

00:38:25.369 --> 00:38:27.838
but it worked much
better as a lash primer.

00:38:27.838 --> 00:38:30.341
I also tried the Blushin Like cream blush.

00:38:30.341 --> 00:38:32.476
It's supposed to be a
cream-to-powder formula,

00:38:32.476 --> 00:38:34.345
but it just kind of feels like a powder.

00:38:34.345 --> 00:38:36.347
I used my sponge to apply it at first,

00:38:36.347 --> 00:38:38.516
but it just kind of
looked a little splotchy.

00:38:38.516 --> 00:38:40.518
It worked much better with a brush.

00:38:40.518 --> 00:38:41.986
You can also apply it to the lips,

00:38:41.986 --> 00:38:43.187
and it was honestly cute.

00:38:43.187 --> 00:38:44.755
It's buildable, which I like,

00:38:44.755 --> 00:38:46.924
but I don't feel like
this is anything special.

00:38:46.924 --> 00:38:49.293
ColourPop drops new stuff,
like, every other day,

00:38:49.293 --> 00:38:51.729
but these Graphix ink
liners caught my eye.

00:38:51.729 --> 00:38:55.466
I really like this tip. I's
supersharp and flexible.

00:38:55.466 --> 00:38:58.169
I am horrible at doing any
kind of liner situation,

00:38:58.169 --> 00:38:59.236
so I was really glad

00:38:59.236 --> 00:39:01.706
that this tip kind of did the work for me.

00:39:01.706 --> 00:39:05.876
However, the color payoff
on these is not great.

00:39:05.876 --> 00:39:07.745
I found myself layering up the product

00:39:07.745 --> 00:39:10.081
for full color payoff,
and with this formula,

00:39:10.081 --> 00:39:13.217
the more you layer, the
more textured it looks.

00:39:13.217 --> 00:39:14.819
It sucks because these are colors

00:39:14.819 --> 00:39:17.154
that I don't really see
a lot of in eyeliner,

00:39:17.154 --> 00:39:19.690
but this formula is just not my favorite.

00:39:19.690 --> 00:39:21.325
IT Cosmetics just dropped another

00:39:21.325 --> 00:39:22.860
Love is the Foundation brush.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:25.196
I think it drops one of these a year.

00:39:25.196 --> 00:39:27.732
I have one from a previous
year that I really love,

00:39:27.732 --> 00:39:29.567
but they're actually not the same.

00:39:29.567 --> 00:39:31.202
This new one is less dense

00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:32.870
and more flexible than my old one,

00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:34.438
and I also feel like the bristles

00:39:34.438 --> 00:39:36.207
on this new one are longer.

00:39:36.207 --> 00:39:37.875
I used it to apply my foundation,

00:39:37.875 --> 00:39:39.577
and I was really happy with how fast

00:39:39.577 --> 00:39:42.646
it blended everything in
without looking streaky.

00:39:42.646 --> 00:39:44.648
It also worked great with my concealer.

00:39:44.648 --> 00:39:46.517
I didn't lose any coverage with this brush

00:39:46.517 --> 00:39:48.219
because it didn't absorb the product.

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:49.854
I think I actually like this new one

00:39:49.854 --> 00:39:51.355
better than my old one.

00:39:51.355 --> 00:39:53.724
I tried a couple of
products from J.Cat Beauty.

00:39:53.724 --> 00:39:55.826
Let's talk about this blush first.

00:39:55.826 --> 00:39:57.561
This color is so pretty.

00:39:57.561 --> 00:39:58.796
It's like an orangey pink

00:39:58.796 --> 00:40:00.331
with a bunch of gold shimmer in it,

00:40:00.331 --> 00:40:02.366
so you get this very buildable color

00:40:02.366 --> 00:40:03.901
with some added glow.

00:40:03.901 --> 00:40:05.803
I can definitely see this color working

00:40:05.803 --> 00:40:08.005
for so many different skin tones.

00:40:08.005 --> 00:40:10.074
The Mood Flick holo-sparkle lip balm

00:40:10.074 --> 00:40:12.510
is one of those
color-changing lip products.

00:40:12.510 --> 00:40:14.512
I honestly thought these
would be more glittery,

00:40:14.512 --> 00:40:16.647
but I think it just looked metallic on me.

00:40:16.647 --> 00:40:19.483
They do actually feel pretty
moisturizing on the lips.

00:40:19.483 --> 00:40:22.086
I was really surprised
at how much these stain.

00:40:22.086 --> 00:40:23.587
When I was trying to take it off,

00:40:23.587 --> 00:40:25.156
my lips were bright pink.

00:40:25.156 --> 00:40:26.824
I don't know if I'd ever use these again,

00:40:26.824 --> 00:40:27.725
but they're cute.

00:40:27.725 --> 00:40:30.961
I haven't reviewed a Too
Faced product in forever,

00:40:30.961 --> 00:40:32.129
but it just released this

00:40:32.129 --> 00:40:35.332
Born This Way Ethereal
Light smoothing concealer,

00:40:35.332 --> 00:40:37.401
and I heard really good things about it.

00:40:37.401 --> 00:40:40.271
It's supposed to be super
hydrating and smoothing.

00:40:40.271 --> 00:40:42.339
I did not like the applicator on this,

00:40:42.339 --> 00:40:43.340
not because of the shape,

00:40:43.340 --> 00:40:45.743
but because it doesn't
pick up product that well.

00:40:45.743 --> 00:40:47.845
This formula is actually really nice.

00:40:47.845 --> 00:40:50.247
Even after blending it out
and setting it with powder,

00:40:50.247 --> 00:40:53.317
you can still see that
luminosity in the concealer.

00:40:53.317 --> 00:40:54.819
I don't know if it did much smoothing,

00:40:54.819 --> 00:40:56.187
but I like the coverage it gave me

00:40:56.187 --> 00:40:58.022
and how easy it was to work with.

00:40:58.022 --> 00:41:00.591
This is the Dior Rouge Dior Forever

00:41:00.591 --> 00:41:02.259
transfer-proof lipstick.

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:05.129
Not a liquid lipstick, a regular lipstick.

00:41:05.129 --> 00:41:07.498
So you apply this like any other lipstick,

00:41:07.498 --> 00:41:09.500
wait three minutes for the color to set,

00:41:09.500 --> 00:41:10.501
and you should be left

00:41:10.501 --> 00:41:12.803
with a long-wearing, transfer-proof lip.

00:41:12.803 --> 00:41:15.206
I think this particular
shade was a bit patchy,

00:41:15.206 --> 00:41:17.475
but I evened it out as much as I could.

00:41:17.475 --> 00:41:19.610
I could not believe how well this worked.

00:41:19.610 --> 00:41:21.512
I was expecting a lot of transfer

00:41:21.512 --> 00:41:23.514
because this is a regular lipstick,

00:41:23.514 --> 00:41:25.549
but the transfer was pretty minimal.

00:41:25.549 --> 00:41:28.252
It also didn't feel
too drying on the lips.

00:41:28.252 --> 00:41:30.120
I think this formula is really cool,

00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:31.922
and I want to try out some other shades.

00:41:31.922 --> 00:41:33.557
I finally got my hands on

00:41:33.557 --> 00:41:36.160
the Haus Labs Atomic Shake lip lacquer.

00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:38.095
This is another one of
those transfer-proof

00:41:38.095 --> 00:41:39.697
glossy lipsticks.

00:41:39.697 --> 00:41:42.166
This is definitely the
hot new lip formula.

00:41:42.166 --> 00:41:44.902
So, you shake the product
well, then apply it.

00:41:44.902 --> 00:41:47.471
The pigment in this really shocked me.

00:41:47.471 --> 00:41:50.407
It was so vibrant, it almost looked neon.

00:41:50.407 --> 00:41:51.842
This went on so smooth,

00:41:51.842 --> 00:41:54.178
I didn't need more than one
layer for full coverage,

00:41:54.178 --> 00:41:55.880
and it was so glossy.

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:57.348
I had to wait 15 seconds

00:41:57.348 --> 00:41:59.617
for what they call the
"shine shield" to form.

00:41:59.617 --> 00:42:01.018
Then I kissed the back of my hand

00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:04.054
to see if I got any transfer, and nothing.

00:42:04.054 --> 00:42:06.223
I've tried three lipsticks
with this kind of formula,

00:42:06.223 --> 00:42:07.958
and so far, this is the best one.

00:42:07.958 --> 00:42:11.061
This is the Modelones Color
Cube in Bonfire Amour.

00:42:11.061 --> 00:42:12.997
It's a solid gel cream palette.

00:42:12.997 --> 00:42:14.632
It comes with nine gel polishes,

00:42:14.632 --> 00:42:16.567
and you can get them in
different color stories

00:42:16.567 --> 00:42:17.635
and finishes.

00:42:17.635 --> 00:42:19.603
It also comes with this little brush.

00:42:19.603 --> 00:42:21.705
I've used a solid gel cream before,

00:42:21.705 --> 00:42:24.008
but I forgot how thick it actually is,

00:42:24.008 --> 00:42:27.545
so it did take me some time
to apply it in even layers.

00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:28.746
I did have to do two coats

00:42:28.746 --> 00:42:30.648
for full coverage on some colors.

00:42:30.648 --> 00:42:32.950
I think a product like this
can be super convenient,

00:42:32.950 --> 00:42:35.486
especially if you do nail art
or just don't have the space

00:42:35.486 --> 00:42:37.721
to keep a bunch of gel polishes around.

00:42:37.721 --> 00:42:39.456
It doesn't come with a base or topcoat,

00:42:39.456 --> 00:42:41.292
but I still really like this.

00:42:41.292 --> 00:42:44.328
I tested out a ton of
products from Jason Wu Beauty.

00:42:44.328 --> 00:42:45.563
This is a new brand for me,

00:42:45.563 --> 00:42:47.631
so let's start with what I didn't like.

00:42:47.631 --> 00:42:50.734
This Free-Da Brow was too light
for me, which is my fault,

00:42:50.734 --> 00:42:52.736
but the formula on this is weird.

00:42:52.736 --> 00:42:55.573
It feels like an oily cream
that never dries down,

00:42:55.573 --> 00:42:57.875
so I doubt it'll keep my brows in place.

00:42:57.875 --> 00:43:00.277
These Stay in Line lip
liners weren't great.

00:43:00.277 --> 00:43:01.712
They were also too light for me,

00:43:01.712 --> 00:43:04.515
so I ended up using my own
lip liner to deepen it.

00:43:04.515 --> 00:43:06.817
These are smooth but a little too creamy.

00:43:06.817 --> 00:43:07.918
They don't feel like they're going to

00:43:07.918 --> 00:43:10.154
last very long on the lips at all.

00:43:10.154 --> 00:43:12.456
I also didn't like the Wu-Prime Eye.

00:43:12.456 --> 00:43:15.492
The formula is so tacky and thick.

00:43:15.492 --> 00:43:18.495
It made my eye shadow look
patchy in certain areas.

00:43:18.495 --> 00:43:20.698
Now on to the stuff I loved.

00:43:20.698 --> 00:43:23.834
This Flora 4 palette was
surprisingly pigmented

00:43:23.834 --> 00:43:25.035
and easy to blend.

00:43:25.035 --> 00:43:27.037
I feel like the primer
is what got in the way

00:43:27.037 --> 00:43:28.706
of showing you its full potential,

00:43:28.706 --> 00:43:30.574
but I still really liked it.

00:43:30.574 --> 00:43:32.776
This blush trio is so gorgeous

00:43:32.776 --> 00:43:34.411
and blended out really nicely.

00:43:34.411 --> 00:43:37.815
I used this Ready to Shimmer
cream shadow as a highlighter,

00:43:37.815 --> 00:43:40.084
and it gave me the prettiest golden glow,

00:43:40.084 --> 00:43:42.353
even though it's not
really meant for the face.

00:43:42.353 --> 00:43:44.455
This Jewel Stick was incredible.

00:43:44.455 --> 00:43:46.624
Look how much it brightened
up my inner corners.

00:43:46.624 --> 00:43:47.791
The Honey Fluff lip cream

00:43:47.791 --> 00:43:50.160
was soft and comfortable on the lips.

00:43:51.495 --> 00:43:53.864
If you get anything from this brand,

00:43:53.864 --> 00:43:56.233
get this Extra Pout lip plumper.

00:43:56.233 --> 00:43:57.868
Oh, my God. Even if you don't care

00:43:57.868 --> 00:43:59.269
about the lip-plumping aspect,

00:43:59.269 --> 00:44:01.338
this is one of the best lip-gloss formulas

00:44:01.338 --> 00:44:02.640
I have ever tried.

00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:05.275
It's so cushiony and shiny and amazing,

00:44:05.275 --> 00:44:06.810
and everyone should get it.

00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:09.313
The Make Up For Ever The
Professionall Mascara

00:44:09.313 --> 00:44:11.715
is ... definitely a mascara.

00:44:11.715 --> 00:44:12.916
It's nothing amazing.

00:44:12.916 --> 00:44:14.385
It has one side for lifting

00:44:14.385 --> 00:44:16.387
and the other side for volumizing.

00:44:16.387 --> 00:44:17.655
I didn't get much of a lift,

00:44:17.655 --> 00:44:19.790
but I did get a nice amount of volume.

00:44:19.790 --> 00:44:21.592
I just think there are
better mascaras out there

00:44:21.592 --> 00:44:22.726
for way less money.

00:44:22.726 --> 00:44:24.695
I am a huge fan of About-Face.

00:44:24.695 --> 00:44:26.296
I love so many of its products.

00:44:26.296 --> 00:44:28.465
So when these Cheek Freak
blush balms dropped,

00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:30.734
I snatched up three different colors.

00:44:30.734 --> 00:44:31.969
I'm just gonna say it.

00:44:31.969 --> 00:44:34.538
I am so in love with these.

00:44:34.538 --> 00:44:35.939
I was nervous at first

00:44:35.939 --> 00:44:38.108
because it's described as a "blush balm,"

00:44:38.108 --> 00:44:41.278
which to me sounded like it
would break up my foundation,

00:44:41.278 --> 00:44:43.947
but these blended in so beautifully.

00:44:43.947 --> 00:44:45.616
It never moved the product underneath,

00:44:45.616 --> 00:44:47.685
even if my skin was already powdered,

00:44:47.685 --> 00:44:49.753
and the pigment on these is unreal.

00:44:49.753 --> 00:44:51.955
You can build them up
however much you want.

00:44:51.955 --> 00:44:54.625
I think these can work for
so many different skin tones.

00:44:54.625 --> 00:44:56.460
They are so, so good.

00:44:56.460 --> 00:44:58.595
I made the horrible mistake of purchasing

00:44:58.595 --> 00:45:02.433
the Winky Lux Saucy Gloss
four-piece combo lip-gloss set.

00:45:02.433 --> 00:45:05.135
This was made in
collaboration with Applebee's,

00:45:05.135 --> 00:45:08.172
and the glosses are
inspired by its wing sauces.

00:45:08.172 --> 00:45:10.674
You guys, I thought
everyone was exaggerating

00:45:10.674 --> 00:45:14.211
when they said the smell
was making them gag, but no.

00:45:14.211 --> 00:45:17.181
These smell God-awful, and it sucks so bad

00:45:17.181 --> 00:45:19.516
because the color story is so pretty.

00:45:19.516 --> 00:45:21.885
And I could see this concept working

00:45:21.885 --> 00:45:25.422
had they just not added the sauce scents,

00:45:25.422 --> 00:45:26.990
or even if they did something like,

00:45:26.990 --> 00:45:28.792
lemon pepper smells like lemon,

00:45:28.792 --> 00:45:31.095
Buffalo is just a spicy lip plumper.

00:45:31.095 --> 00:45:33.430
But no, they went in this direction.

00:45:33.430 --> 00:45:35.199
We all bought it and talked about it,

00:45:35.199 --> 00:45:36.834
which is probably what they wanted.

00:45:36.834 --> 00:45:39.136
So I hope you're happy, Winky Lux.

00:45:39.136 --> 00:45:41.805
You ruined four beautiful glosses.

00:45:41.805 --> 00:45:44.041
I tried out a new foundation from Chanel.

00:45:44.041 --> 00:45:46.243
I actually wouldn't
call this a foundation.

00:45:46.243 --> 00:45:49.747
It's more like a
super-hydrating, light tint.

00:45:49.747 --> 00:45:52.683
It's very similar to that
Rose Inc tinted serum

00:45:52.683 --> 00:45:54.151
I tried a while ago.

00:45:54.151 --> 00:45:56.520
So it has these pigment beads that burst

00:45:56.520 --> 00:45:58.355
and spread as you apply it.

00:45:58.355 --> 00:46:01.158
This literally feels
like nothing on the skin.

00:46:01.158 --> 00:46:02.493
There is little coverage,

00:46:02.493 --> 00:46:05.896
but it evens everything out
nicely and it feels hydrating.

00:46:05.896 --> 00:46:07.998
I don't think this has
a strong staying power,

00:46:07.998 --> 00:46:09.233
but it's still a pretty tint

00:46:09.233 --> 00:46:11.301
for when you don't want to do too much.

00:46:11.301 --> 00:46:13.537
Chanel also has a blush in this formula,

00:46:13.537 --> 00:46:15.172
so I tested that out too.

00:46:15.172 --> 00:46:17.374
I actually blended it out
on the back of my hand

00:46:17.374 --> 00:46:19.877
before applying and tapped
it on with a sponge.

00:46:19.877 --> 00:46:21.478
It took a minute to build up the color,

00:46:21.478 --> 00:46:23.914
but I think it's supposed
to look very natural.

00:46:23.914 --> 00:46:26.283
It also didn't break up
the product underneath.

00:46:26.283 --> 00:46:28.318
I'm surprised by how much I liked these.

00:46:28.318 --> 00:46:29.253
They don't do too much,

00:46:29.253 --> 00:46:31.088
but it's enough to make a difference.

00:46:31.088 --> 00:46:33.924
This is the Maybelline Shadow
Blocks Eyeshadow Palette.

00:46:33.924 --> 00:46:35.692
It's a tiny stack of eye shadows,

00:46:35.692 --> 00:46:38.629
very similar to the Kaja bento trios.

00:46:38.629 --> 00:46:40.397
The packaging is pretty cheap.

00:46:40.397 --> 00:46:42.633
One of my shadows fell out, but it's OK.

00:46:42.633 --> 00:46:44.401
I applied these without any primer

00:46:44.401 --> 00:46:46.537
just to see how they perform on their own.

00:46:46.537 --> 00:46:48.906
They're actually pretty pigmented shadows.

00:46:48.906 --> 00:46:50.340
I didn't have any trouble blending them,

00:46:50.340 --> 00:46:51.842
and the shimmer shade was pretty,

00:46:51.842 --> 00:46:53.944
but overall I think these are just OK.

00:46:53.944 --> 00:46:55.679
I like the idea of a palette like this

00:46:55.679 --> 00:46:57.214
more than the execution.

00:46:57.214 --> 00:47:00.384
Everyone has been loving
these NYX Jumbo Lash lashes,

00:47:00.384 --> 00:47:01.552
so I had to try them

00:47:01.552 --> 00:47:04.121
even though I am terrible
with false lashes.

00:47:04.121 --> 00:47:05.522
I thought the style Ego Flare

00:47:05.522 --> 00:47:08.091
would look nice on my eye
shape, and I was right.

00:47:08.091 --> 00:47:10.661
These lashes made me feel
like a whole new person.

00:47:10.661 --> 00:47:12.830
Like, these are Disney princess eyes.

00:47:12.830 --> 00:47:14.231
They were pretty easy to apply,

00:47:14.231 --> 00:47:15.866
and the band was really comfortable.

00:47:15.866 --> 00:47:17.568
I think these have totally convinced me

00:47:17.568 --> 00:47:19.203
to wear lashes more often.

00:47:19.203 --> 00:47:22.172
This is the Urban Decay
24/7 Moondust Shadow

00:47:22.172 --> 00:47:23.640
in Space Cowboy.

00:47:23.640 --> 00:47:25.843
This is basically a glitter shadow.

00:47:25.843 --> 00:47:28.178
This shade in particular
has been going viral.

00:47:28.178 --> 00:47:30.781
It is super intense and reflective,

00:47:30.781 --> 00:47:33.584
but you can definitely
diffuse it to be more subtle.

00:47:33.584 --> 00:47:36.019
This formula is really
smooth and easy to work with

00:47:36.019 --> 00:47:39.022
however you want to use
it, so I really loved this.

00:47:39.022 --> 00:47:40.424
I did get some glitter fallout,

00:47:40.424 --> 00:47:41.925
so I'd recommend using a primer

00:47:41.925 --> 00:47:44.895
or leaving some powder under
the eyes while you're applying.

00:47:44.895 --> 00:47:46.663
If you want something more eye-catching

00:47:46.663 --> 00:47:49.700
and elevated than a shimmer
shadow, this is perfect.

00:47:49.700 --> 00:47:52.669
Em Cosmetics re-released
its Color Drops Serum Blush

00:47:52.669 --> 00:47:55.205
with a new-and-improved
formula and packaging.

00:47:55.205 --> 00:47:58.442
The old packaging was
notoriously difficult to use.

00:47:58.442 --> 00:47:59.610
It had this dropper thing

00:47:59.610 --> 00:48:02.079
that just would not dispense properly.

00:48:02.079 --> 00:48:04.081
This new dropper is so much better.

00:48:04.081 --> 00:48:05.682
You do have to build this blush up,

00:48:05.682 --> 00:48:08.619
but it gives you a really
pretty, dewy flush of color.

00:48:08.619 --> 00:48:09.953
I honestly can't see a difference

00:48:09.953 --> 00:48:11.955
between the old formula and the new one,

00:48:11.955 --> 00:48:14.024
this new one is just easier to use.

00:48:14.024 --> 00:48:16.393
I'm not super into this
kind of blush formula.

00:48:16.393 --> 00:48:19.396
I prefer the brand's powder
or cream blush over this.

00:48:19.396 --> 00:48:21.932
But it's pretty, and it
didn't break up my foundation.

00:48:21.932 --> 00:48:23.400
I've been dying to test out

00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:24.935
the new Haus Labs foundation,

00:48:24.935 --> 00:48:26.803
I've heard nothing but amazing things,

00:48:26.803 --> 00:48:29.106
and I was not disappointed.

00:48:29.106 --> 00:48:31.141
I went in with my foundation brush first,

00:48:31.141 --> 00:48:34.544
and this just totally blends
into the skin seamlessly.

00:48:34.544 --> 00:48:36.413
The coverage is on the lighter side,

00:48:36.413 --> 00:48:37.614
so I added a little more,

00:48:37.614 --> 00:48:40.417
and I am really impressed
by how weightless it is.

00:48:40.417 --> 00:48:42.119
It has skincare ingredients in it,

00:48:42.119 --> 00:48:44.454
and it actually feels like skincare.

00:48:44.454 --> 00:48:47.124
It feels like you have
absolutely nothing on your face.

00:48:47.124 --> 00:48:48.125
All of my other products

00:48:48.125 --> 00:48:49.826
blended on top of this beautifully.

00:48:49.826 --> 00:48:52.262
So this foundation is
a 10 out of 10 for me.

00:48:52.262 --> 00:48:54.932
I also got the Bio-Blurring
Loose Setting Powder,

00:48:54.932 --> 00:48:56.333
and I love this too.

00:48:56.333 --> 00:48:59.069
It definitely does blur the
skin and sets your makeup

00:48:59.069 --> 00:49:01.271
without making it look dry or cakey.

00:49:01.271 --> 00:49:03.106
It's so soft and finely milled,

00:49:03.106 --> 00:49:05.142
and it's also talc-free, which is great.

00:49:05.142 --> 00:49:07.244
I tried a couple lip
products from Fenty Beauty,

00:49:07.244 --> 00:49:10.013
the Gloss Bomb Heat Universal
Lip Luminizer and Plumper

00:49:10.013 --> 00:49:11.248
in Hot Chocolit Heat

00:49:11.248 --> 00:49:13.583
and the Gloss Bomb Ice
Cooling Lip Luminizer

00:49:13.583 --> 00:49:14.685
in Cold Heart'd.

00:49:14.685 --> 00:49:17.654
Let's talk about this
new Gloss Bomb Ice first.

00:49:17.654 --> 00:49:19.323
It looks like a pale blue color,

00:49:19.323 --> 00:49:21.091
but it goes on totally clear.

00:49:21.091 --> 00:49:23.493
It has a really nice minty scent.

00:49:23.493 --> 00:49:26.530
You get that cooling effect
instantly, and I like it.

00:49:26.530 --> 00:49:28.165
It also feels great on the lips,

00:49:28.165 --> 00:49:29.666
like the other Fenty glosses,

00:49:29.666 --> 00:49:31.935
just super hydrating and shiny.

00:49:31.935 --> 00:49:33.937
The Gloss Bomb Heat is not a new formula,

00:49:33.937 --> 00:49:34.938
but people have been loving

00:49:34.938 --> 00:49:36.506
the Hot Chocolit Heat shade.

00:49:36.506 --> 00:49:39.343
It's like a brown with a
hint of rosiness to it.

00:49:39.343 --> 00:49:41.144
Because it's on the more sheer side,

00:49:41.144 --> 00:49:42.679
this color looks incredible

00:49:42.679 --> 00:49:44.514
on so many different skin tones,

00:49:44.514 --> 00:49:47.184
and it actually does plump
the lips really nicely.

00:49:47.184 --> 00:49:50.020
It's not an uncomfortable
plumping effect at all.

00:49:50.020 --> 00:49:52.556
A few of you asked if I could
review Mooncat polishes,

00:49:52.556 --> 00:49:54.224
so I have a few to talk about.

00:49:54.224 --> 00:49:56.293
This first one is called Illusionist,

00:49:56.293 --> 00:49:58.128
and it's a magnetic multichrome.

00:49:58.128 --> 00:49:59.830
I feel like Mooncat always has

00:49:59.830 --> 00:50:02.232
these really interesting colors like this

00:50:02.232 --> 00:50:04.167
that I don't see very often.

00:50:04.167 --> 00:50:06.636
The magnetic effect on
this one is so cool.

00:50:06.636 --> 00:50:08.638
I couldn't stop staring at my nails.

00:50:08.638 --> 00:50:10.307
This next shade is called Cyclone,

00:50:10.307 --> 00:50:12.676
and it's a blue-jelly flaky polish.

00:50:12.676 --> 00:50:15.312
The way these iridescent
flakes look in this jelly

00:50:15.312 --> 00:50:17.381
really give you this ocean vibe,

00:50:17.381 --> 00:50:18.915
so I loved this one too.

00:50:18.915 --> 00:50:21.251
The last polish I tried was Emo for Life,

00:50:21.251 --> 00:50:23.820
which is just a plain black crème polish.

00:50:23.820 --> 00:50:26.223
I honestly feel like this
one impressed me the most,

00:50:26.223 --> 00:50:29.659
because it was literally
pitch black in one coat.

00:50:29.659 --> 00:50:31.328
The pigment on it is incredible,

00:50:31.328 --> 00:50:33.363
and the formula is so smooth.

00:50:33.363 --> 00:50:35.665
The prices do vary
depending on the formula,

00:50:35.665 --> 00:50:38.735
but overall, the quality of
the polish is really good,

00:50:38.735 --> 00:50:41.271
and I also love the brush
and handle on these bottles.

00:50:41.271 --> 00:50:43.407
They make it super easy to paint my nails.

00:50:43.407 --> 00:50:45.575
This is the Charlotte
Tilbury Take It All Off.

00:50:45.575 --> 00:50:47.511
It's a biphase makeup remover,

00:50:47.511 --> 00:50:48.678
and I had to Google what that meant,

00:50:48.678 --> 00:50:50.280
because I had no idea.

00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:53.050
It basically means you get
an oil and water in one,

00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:55.285
and you have to shake the
product to combine it.

00:50:55.285 --> 00:50:58.789
It specifically says this is
for eyes, lashes, and lips.

00:50:58.789 --> 00:51:01.024
You have to shake it,
apply it to a cotton pad,

00:51:01.024 --> 00:51:04.294
and soak the area for a few
seconds for an easy removal.

00:51:04.294 --> 00:51:05.862
This honestly worked really well,

00:51:05.862 --> 00:51:07.697
and I tried it on waterproof mascara,

00:51:07.697 --> 00:51:09.766
which always takes me forever to remove.

00:51:09.766 --> 00:51:11.468
I also have very sensitive eyes,

00:51:11.468 --> 00:51:12.903
and this didn't irritate them at all.

00:51:12.903 --> 00:51:15.272
I liked this, but I think
it's a little too pricey

00:51:15.272 --> 00:51:17.541
for a makeup remover
you're only supposed to use

00:51:17.541 --> 00:51:18.708
on your eyes and lips.-

00:51:18.708 --> 00:51:20.577
Saie just drop these Lip Blurs.

00:51:20.577 --> 00:51:22.546
They're matte lipsticks
that you can build up

00:51:22.546 --> 00:51:23.780
to be super-full coverage

00:51:23.780 --> 00:51:26.249
or dab on for a soft, blurred lip.

00:51:26.249 --> 00:51:27.784
I used the shade Modern first

00:51:27.784 --> 00:51:29.419
and just dabbed it on with my finger.

00:51:29.419 --> 00:51:32.222
It gave this really
pretty soft wash of color.

00:51:32.222 --> 00:51:34.758
This other one, in the shade
Classic, really shocked me

00:51:34.758 --> 00:51:37.561
because it's so smooth and pigmented.

00:51:37.561 --> 00:51:39.563
I was laughing because I
definitely went too far

00:51:39.563 --> 00:51:41.231
over my lip line, but we move.

00:51:41.231 --> 00:51:42.933
I would recommend a lip liner with these,

00:51:42.933 --> 00:51:46.169
because the formula isn't
as matte as you'd expect

00:51:46.169 --> 00:51:47.804
and it does move around a little.

00:51:47.804 --> 00:51:49.272
Overall, I think these are nice

00:51:49.272 --> 00:51:50.507
and feel good on the lips.

00:51:50.507 --> 00:51:52.442
This is the KimChi Chic Beauty

00:51:52.442 --> 00:51:55.278
Pearl Gone Wild pressed
shimmer highlighter.

00:51:55.278 --> 00:51:57.948
This highlighter is so
stunning in the pan.

00:51:57.948 --> 00:52:00.317
It's like this iridescent pearl color

00:52:00.317 --> 00:52:01.852
that shifts to blue.

00:52:01.852 --> 00:52:03.253
There's a lot of glitter in this,

00:52:03.253 --> 00:52:05.956
which can look chunky or
make your skin look textured,

00:52:05.956 --> 00:52:07.991
but this actually went on beautifully.

00:52:07.991 --> 00:52:10.460
The glow it gives is unreal,

00:52:10.460 --> 00:52:13.130
and that blue sparkle adds
a little something special.

00:52:13.130 --> 00:52:14.598
It's not going to be for everyone,

00:52:14.598 --> 00:52:16.133
especially if you hate glitter,

00:52:16.133 --> 00:52:17.834
but this formula is so pretty,

00:52:17.834 --> 00:52:19.736
and I really want more colors.

00:52:19.736 --> 00:52:21.671
Patrick Ta released these Major Skin

00:52:21.671 --> 00:52:24.107
crème foundation and
finishing powder duos.

00:52:24.107 --> 00:52:25.542
I love the packaging on this,

00:52:25.542 --> 00:52:26.943
especially this little flap

00:52:26.943 --> 00:52:28.912
to protect the foundation from the powder.

00:52:28.912 --> 00:52:30.814
I went in with my foundation brush first,

00:52:30.814 --> 00:52:32.916
and, wow, this is full coverage,

00:52:32.916 --> 00:52:34.217
and a little goes a long way.

00:52:34.217 --> 00:52:37.787
I did my entire face with
just one dip into the pan.

00:52:37.787 --> 00:52:40.557
I went over that with a sponge
to pick up excess product.

00:52:40.557 --> 00:52:43.093
I wouldn't say the finish
is super skin-like.

00:52:43.093 --> 00:52:44.761
It definitely looks and feels

00:52:44.761 --> 00:52:46.329
like you're wearing foundation.

00:52:46.329 --> 00:52:47.864
But for something this full coverage,

00:52:47.864 --> 00:52:49.366
it doesn't look cakey to me.

00:52:49.366 --> 00:52:51.902
It's also a more dewy
finish, which I think helps.

00:52:51.902 --> 00:52:53.203
These are the Uoma Beauty

00:52:53.203 --> 00:52:56.006
Black Magic Hypnotic Impact
high-shine lipsticks.

00:52:56.006 --> 00:52:58.975
I am so into shiny lipstick
formulas these days.

00:52:58.975 --> 00:53:01.578
Formula aside though, these
lipsticks are gorgeous.

00:53:01.578 --> 00:53:03.013
The embossing, the glitter,

00:53:03.013 --> 00:53:05.115
I could not stop staring at them.

00:53:05.115 --> 00:53:06.917
They look just as beautiful on the lips.

00:53:06.917 --> 00:53:10.053
This formula is literally a
lip gloss in lipstick form,

00:53:10.053 --> 00:53:11.121
so you get the shine

00:53:11.121 --> 00:53:13.256
and you get that moisturizing feeling.

00:53:13.256 --> 00:53:14.658
The glitter is an overspray,

00:53:14.658 --> 00:53:16.393
so they don't look glittery on the lips,

00:53:16.393 --> 00:53:17.561
but I love these.

00:53:17.561 --> 00:53:19.196
This is the Merit Bronze Balm,

00:53:19.196 --> 00:53:21.731
and it's supposedly the
"easiest bronzer ever."

00:53:21.731 --> 00:53:23.533
It's definitely the easiest bronzer

00:53:23.533 --> 00:53:25.101
I think I've ever used.

00:53:25.101 --> 00:53:27.504
It takes little to no
effort to blend this out,

00:53:27.504 --> 00:53:29.906
and it didn't break up the
product I already had on.

00:53:29.906 --> 00:53:31.808
I was worried the shade
I got was too light,

00:53:31.808 --> 00:53:33.710
but I think it actually turned out OK.

00:53:33.710 --> 00:53:37.080
It is buildable, I just wish
the color wasn't so sheer.

00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:38.882
Other than that, I like this.

00:53:38.882 --> 00:53:40.817
I'm seeing transfer-proof bullet lipsticks

00:53:40.817 --> 00:53:42.385
pop up a lot more lately.

00:53:42.385 --> 00:53:44.888
This one is the Nars Powermatte lipstick.

00:53:44.888 --> 00:53:47.090
It has a really amazing color payoff.

00:53:47.090 --> 00:53:49.593
This can definitely be
a one-swipe lipstick.

00:53:49.593 --> 00:53:51.494
The texture is so unique.

00:53:51.494 --> 00:53:53.797
The best way I can describe it is that it

00:53:53.797 --> 00:53:56.700
kind of feels like the
Nars soft matte packaging

00:53:56.700 --> 00:53:59.135
on its products, but on your lips.

00:53:59.135 --> 00:54:02.172
It's this soft, powdery,
comfortable kind of matte

00:54:02.172 --> 00:54:03.907
that felt really nice on the lips,

00:54:03.907 --> 00:54:06.743
and it is transfer-proof,
so I highly recommend this.

00:54:06.743 --> 00:54:09.479
This is the REM Beauty
Space Shape brow gel.

00:54:09.479 --> 00:54:11.448
What really drew me in to this product

00:54:11.448 --> 00:54:12.616
was the applicator.

00:54:12.616 --> 00:54:14.517
I've never seen one like this before,

00:54:14.517 --> 00:54:16.519
with a little doe foot on one side

00:54:16.519 --> 00:54:17.954
and a comb on the other.

00:54:17.954 --> 00:54:19.322
It was really easy to use,

00:54:19.322 --> 00:54:21.458
and I like how it distributed the product.

00:54:21.458 --> 00:54:23.126
The actual brow gel is nice.

00:54:23.126 --> 00:54:24.294
It did what it had to do,

00:54:24.294 --> 00:54:26.329
and it didn't leave my
brows feeling crunchy.

00:54:26.329 --> 00:54:28.265
As much as I like the applicator, though,

00:54:28.265 --> 00:54:31.067
I don't feel like the
formula is anything special.

00:54:31.067 --> 00:54:34.271
KVD has reformulated its
iconic liquid lipstick,

00:54:34.271 --> 00:54:36.206
so I picked up a few shades to try.

00:54:36.206 --> 00:54:37.240
Just like everybody else,

00:54:37.240 --> 00:54:40.010
I was very big into the
shade Lolita back in the day,

00:54:40.010 --> 00:54:43.546
so I had to get Queen of
Poisons, which is its new name.

00:54:43.546 --> 00:54:44.581
I'm gonna be honest.

00:54:44.581 --> 00:54:46.283
I can't really tell much of a difference

00:54:46.283 --> 00:54:48.485
between this formula and the old one.

00:54:48.485 --> 00:54:50.787
I think it maybe feels a
little more lightweight,

00:54:50.787 --> 00:54:52.188
but it still feels like I'm wearing

00:54:52.188 --> 00:54:54.257
a slightly drying liquid lipstick.

00:54:54.257 --> 00:54:55.792
I do really like the colors I got,

00:54:55.792 --> 00:54:57.927
but this bright orange was pretty patchy.

00:54:57.927 --> 00:54:59.763
I actually remember
having the same problem

00:54:59.763 --> 00:55:02.032
with the brighter colors
in the old formula too,

00:55:02.032 --> 00:55:03.033
so that's not great.

00:55:03.033 --> 00:55:04.834
I also don't like this new packaging.

00:55:04.834 --> 00:55:06.469
The wand is so weirdly long.

00:55:06.469 --> 00:55:07.671
I don't know if you can tell,

00:55:07.671 --> 00:55:10.040
but it was kind of hard to
control when I was applying.

00:55:10.040 --> 00:55:11.775
I have been dying to try these Versed

00:55:11.775 --> 00:55:14.611
Mood Lighting Luminizing
Glow Drops for a while.

00:55:14.611 --> 00:55:17.113
People say that this is
another Flawless Filter dupe.

00:55:17.113 --> 00:55:19.582
It does give a really
beautiful glow to the skin,

00:55:19.582 --> 00:55:21.518
but there's not really any coverage to it,

00:55:21.518 --> 00:55:23.920
so I wouldn't call this a dupe exactly.

00:55:23.920 --> 00:55:27.257
It's like Flawless Filter's
more natural little sister.

00:55:27.257 --> 00:55:29.392
It has a lot of great skincare ingredients

00:55:29.392 --> 00:55:31.961
that made my skin feel
really nice and hydrated.

00:55:31.961 --> 00:55:34.364
I actually preferred the
drops under my foundation

00:55:34.364 --> 00:55:36.733
rather than on their own,
but I like these a lot.

00:55:36.733 --> 00:55:38.535
This is a Face Sprinkles mini palette

00:55:38.535 --> 00:55:39.803
from Designer Dust Co.

00:55:39.803 --> 00:55:41.638
They have a lot of different
ones to choose from,

00:55:41.638 --> 00:55:43.306
and you can even make a custom palette

00:55:43.306 --> 00:55:44.607
with any of their glitters.

00:55:44.607 --> 00:55:46.509
I was trying to show all of the colors,

00:55:46.509 --> 00:55:47.644
but I couldn't lift it all the way

00:55:47.644 --> 00:55:50.847
because one of the glitters
was completely liquefied.

00:55:50.847 --> 00:55:53.083
Something weird happened
to it on its way to me,

00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:55.418
but the rest of the
glitters were totally fine.

00:55:55.418 --> 00:55:57.887
The glitter has a vegan
gel base that dries down.

00:55:57.887 --> 00:56:00.323
You can apply it on the
face, hair, or body.

00:56:00.323 --> 00:56:02.258
I was having fun just
putting it everywhere.

00:56:02.258 --> 00:56:03.326
I loved all the colors,

00:56:03.326 --> 00:56:05.128
and it was really easy to apply.

00:56:05.128 --> 00:56:06.496
I'm not really into glitters,

00:56:06.496 --> 00:56:07.731
but I think these worked great,

00:56:07.731 --> 00:56:09.232
and this is one of the more affordable

00:56:09.232 --> 00:56:11.267
glitter gel palettes I've seen.

00:56:11.267 --> 00:56:13.670
This is the Summer
Fridays sheer skin tint.

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:15.772
It's supposed to be
lightweight, hydrating,

00:56:15.772 --> 00:56:17.640
and very natural on the skin.

00:56:17.640 --> 00:56:20.110
I definitely think it
is all of those things.

00:56:20.110 --> 00:56:21.644
The coverage is obviously sheer,

00:56:21.644 --> 00:56:23.813
but I was able to build it up no problem.

00:56:23.813 --> 00:56:25.215
It evened out my skin nicely,

00:56:25.215 --> 00:56:26.783
and it actually does feel weightless.

00:56:26.783 --> 00:56:29.018
This would be a great
everyday skin tint for me.

00:56:29.018 --> 00:56:31.721
I think for what it is and
how little product you get,

00:56:31.721 --> 00:56:33.857
$42 is way too much.

00:56:33.857 --> 00:56:35.692
But if you're looking
for a high-end skin tint,

00:56:35.692 --> 00:56:37.093
this one is really nice.

00:56:37.093 --> 00:56:39.295
I had been getting ads
for this Flower Knows

00:56:39.295 --> 00:56:41.564
Strawberry Rococo collection for weeks,

00:56:41.564 --> 00:56:42.966
and they definitely worked on me

00:56:42.966 --> 00:56:44.934
because I bought three products.

00:56:44.934 --> 00:56:46.903
First up, I tried the embossed blush.

00:56:46.903 --> 00:56:49.372
The detail in the embossing is so cool.

00:56:49.372 --> 00:56:50.840
I didn't even want to use it.

00:56:50.840 --> 00:56:53.476
They do say that this is
meant to be a buildable blush,

00:56:53.476 --> 00:56:55.879
but I think the color payoff
is a little too light.

00:56:55.879 --> 00:56:58.415
It took me forever to get
the color payoff I wanted,

00:56:58.415 --> 00:57:00.316
but it did look pretty in the end.

00:57:00.316 --> 00:57:01.651
On to the eye-shadow palette.

00:57:01.651 --> 00:57:03.820
The matte formula was soft and blendable,

00:57:03.820 --> 00:57:05.989
but next time I would go
in with a primer first,

00:57:05.989 --> 00:57:08.458
because it was slightly
patchy in some areas.

00:57:08.458 --> 00:57:10.193
The glitter shade was incredible.

00:57:10.193 --> 00:57:12.662
It was definitely the best
shade in the entire palette,

00:57:12.662 --> 00:57:14.464
but it did give me some fallout.

00:57:14.464 --> 00:57:16.433
Lastly, I tried the Cloud lip cream.

00:57:16.433 --> 00:57:18.535
This is one of those mousse-y lip formulas

00:57:18.535 --> 00:57:20.136
that has a velvety finish.

00:57:20.136 --> 00:57:22.405
This felt really nice and
comfortable on the lips,

00:57:22.405 --> 00:57:24.040
and I like the blurred effect it gives,

00:57:24.040 --> 00:57:26.976
but I kind of wish it was the
same red as the packaging.

00:57:26.976 --> 00:57:29.612
This is the Caliray So Blown clean primer.

00:57:29.612 --> 00:57:32.649
It's one of those
dimethicone-y blurring primers

00:57:32.649 --> 00:57:34.417
that makes your skin look matte.

00:57:34.417 --> 00:57:36.586
I actually like how it made my skin look

00:57:36.586 --> 00:57:37.921
without any foundation.

00:57:37.921 --> 00:57:39.622
It feels nice and velvety,

00:57:39.622 --> 00:57:41.658
and I definitely saw some blurring.

00:57:41.658 --> 00:57:43.092
When I applied my foundation,

00:57:43.092 --> 00:57:45.228
I realized I applied
too much of the primer,

00:57:45.228 --> 00:57:47.430
so my skin actually
looked kind of textured

00:57:47.430 --> 00:57:49.132
and the product pilled up a bit.

00:57:49.132 --> 00:57:50.400
So the next time I tried it,

00:57:50.400 --> 00:57:53.036
I went in with less and
focused on my oily areas,

00:57:53.036 --> 00:57:54.471
and I still wasn't loving

00:57:54.471 --> 00:57:56.506
how my foundation looked over this.

00:57:56.506 --> 00:57:58.441
I just see way more
texture with this primer

00:57:58.441 --> 00:57:59.776
than my normal primer.

00:57:59.776 --> 00:58:01.010
I'll show them side by side,

00:58:01.010 --> 00:58:02.645
so maybe you can kind of see what I mean.

00:58:02.645 --> 00:58:04.180
I don't think that this is for me.

00:58:04.180 --> 00:58:06.382
Milani released this
Conceal + Perfect line

00:58:06.382 --> 00:58:07.851
with liquid under-eye brighteners,

00:58:07.851 --> 00:58:09.285
contours, and highlighters.

00:58:09.285 --> 00:58:11.054
These kind of feel like
a drugstore version

00:58:11.054 --> 00:58:12.922
of the Charlotte Tilbury wands.

00:58:12.922 --> 00:58:15.058
First, I tried the brightener
under my concealer.

00:58:15.058 --> 00:58:16.793
I didn't notice much brightening at first,

00:58:16.793 --> 00:58:18.595
but then I applied it with my fingertips

00:58:18.595 --> 00:58:20.296
and got some better coverage.

00:58:20.296 --> 00:58:21.998
Next, I tried the liquid contour.

00:58:21.998 --> 00:58:24.567
This color does lean a little
bit red, which I don't love,

00:58:24.567 --> 00:58:26.002
but it blended out really beautifully

00:58:26.002 --> 00:58:28.137
and added a nice warmth to my face.

00:58:28.137 --> 00:58:30.573
I applied the highlighter
next, and I loved this.

00:58:30.573 --> 00:58:32.308
Again, it blends out really nicely,

00:58:32.308 --> 00:58:34.344
and it doesn't add any texture to my skin.

00:58:34.344 --> 00:58:36.379
It just gave a really pretty glow.

00:58:36.379 --> 00:58:38.348
Even though I don't see
myself using the brightener,

00:58:38.348 --> 00:58:39.382
I am a fan of these,

00:58:39.382 --> 00:58:41.317
and I hope they expand the shade range.

00:58:41.317 --> 00:58:43.520
These are the Kaleidos Epiphany Glow

00:58:43.520 --> 00:58:45.822
Melt-On eyeliners.
They're all multichrome,

00:58:45.822 --> 00:58:48.725
so they have these
really cool color shifts.

00:58:48.725 --> 00:58:51.060
"Melt-On" was the perfect
description for these,

00:58:51.060 --> 00:58:53.930
because they really do glide on so easily.

00:58:53.930 --> 00:58:56.266
I've never had such a
smooth eyeliner application,

00:58:56.266 --> 00:58:58.768
because they always
skip or they're too dry.

00:58:58.768 --> 00:59:00.503
These are so easy to apply.

00:59:00.503 --> 00:59:02.205
I thought that the tip would be too blunt

00:59:02.205 --> 00:59:03.706
to create a wing, but I was actually

00:59:03.706 --> 00:59:05.608
able to do it without any issue.

00:59:05.608 --> 00:59:08.177
These are really beautiful,
and I highly recommend them.

00:59:08.177 --> 00:59:09.445
I hope they expand the line

00:59:09.445 --> 00:59:11.681
to include more everyday matte shades.

00:59:11.681 --> 00:59:14.384
This is the Got2b Glued
for brows and edges.

00:59:14.384 --> 00:59:16.185
For a long time, people have been using

00:59:16.185 --> 00:59:17.854
Got2b hair gel as brow gel,

00:59:17.854 --> 00:59:19.222
so they came out with this product

00:59:19.222 --> 00:59:21.090
that's actually meant for brows.

00:59:21.090 --> 00:59:23.192
I actually like how
this made my brows look.

00:59:23.192 --> 00:59:25.562
It gives kind of a laminated brow effect,

00:59:25.562 --> 00:59:26.963
nice and feathery,

00:59:26.963 --> 00:59:29.899
but the gel itself left
a weird residue behind,

00:59:29.899 --> 00:59:31.768
and it took forever to dry down.

00:59:31.768 --> 00:59:34.270
Once it did dry, the brows
pretty much stayed in place,

00:59:34.270 --> 00:59:36.673
but I've definitely
tried better brow gels.

00:59:36.673 --> 00:59:38.708
This is one of the strangest new products

00:59:38.708 --> 00:59:40.410
I've seen in a long time.

00:59:40.410 --> 00:59:43.980
This is a Hipdot Eyecon
Baked Eye Pigment Shadow.

00:59:43.980 --> 00:59:45.548
I got the Share Bear one.

00:59:45.548 --> 00:59:47.717
These are essentially 3D figures

00:59:47.717 --> 00:59:49.586
made of baked eye shadow.

00:59:49.586 --> 00:59:51.888
They kind of feel like makeup Funko pops,

00:59:51.888 --> 00:59:54.958
like more something you
collect rather than use.

00:59:54.958 --> 00:59:55.792
But I used it.

00:59:55.792 --> 00:59:57.760
The formula was actually pretty dry.

00:59:57.760 --> 01:00:00.730
It took me a while to pick
up any product on my brush.

01:00:00.730 --> 01:00:02.565
I definitely got a better application

01:00:02.565 --> 01:00:04.167
and color payoff with my finger,

01:00:04.167 --> 01:00:06.235
but still the formula was dry,

01:00:06.235 --> 01:00:07.704
and I was tugging at my eyelid,

01:00:07.704 --> 01:00:09.305
which I did not like.

01:00:09.305 --> 01:00:10.974
This feels way more like a novelty

01:00:10.974 --> 01:00:12.575
than an actual eye shadow.

01:00:12.575 --> 01:00:14.210
Fenty released this Double Cheek'd Up

01:00:14.210 --> 01:00:15.712
Freestyle Cream Blush Duo.

01:00:15.712 --> 01:00:18.548
So you have this baby pink
color called Mali'booze

01:00:18.548 --> 01:00:21.284
and this deeper medium
pink called Peony Droppa.

01:00:21.284 --> 01:00:23.453
I've heard that the
Fenty cream blush formula

01:00:23.453 --> 01:00:25.088
doesn't have the best color payoff,

01:00:25.088 --> 01:00:26.689
but these were actually pigmented.

01:00:26.689 --> 01:00:29.792
The problems for me
started with application.

01:00:29.792 --> 01:00:31.961
I used a dense brush to apply first,

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:33.563
and it did lift my foundation,

01:00:33.563 --> 01:00:36.466
so I tried my sponge, and
I think I made it worse.

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.501
My face was not powdered, by the way.

01:00:38.501 --> 01:00:40.303
On the other side, I just used my fingers,

01:00:40.303 --> 01:00:43.206
and that also lifted my
foundation, but way less.

01:00:43.206 --> 01:00:44.707
I do really like these shades,

01:00:44.707 --> 01:00:46.909
so I can see myself
using this on bare skin,

01:00:46.909 --> 01:00:48.811
but I am not a fan of this formula

01:00:48.811 --> 01:00:50.246
on top of foundation.

01:00:50.246 --> 01:00:52.148
I finally got my hands on this

01:00:52.148 --> 01:00:54.884
Fourth Ray Beauty Hunny Pot Lip Care Kit.

01:00:54.884 --> 01:00:57.186
It keeps selling out, and now I know why.

01:00:57.186 --> 01:00:59.956
This kit comes with a honey
lip scrub and a lip mask.

01:00:59.956 --> 01:01:02.291
This packaging is literally so cute.

01:01:02.291 --> 01:01:03.893
Look at this tiny honey dipper!

01:01:03.893 --> 01:01:06.062
The scrub is like a regular sugar scrub.

01:01:06.062 --> 01:01:07.930
It made my lips feel really soft,

01:01:07.930 --> 01:01:09.699
but I wish it was a little more coarse

01:01:09.699 --> 01:01:11.934
so I don't have to keep
dipping in for more.

01:01:11.934 --> 01:01:14.337
This lip mask felt incredible.

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:17.273
It's thick and smooth
and really hydrating,

01:01:17.273 --> 01:01:18.908
and it tastes sweet, which I liked.

01:01:18.908 --> 01:01:22.345
This is the Tom Ford Soleil
Neige Lip Blush Lip Balm.

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:23.846
It's this transparent balm

01:01:23.846 --> 01:01:25.848
with a bunch of platinum flecks in it.

01:01:25.848 --> 01:01:27.950
It's actually one of those
color-changing products,

01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.052
so once you apply it,

01:01:29.052 --> 01:01:31.354
it turns into this deep pink shade.

01:01:31.354 --> 01:01:33.556
"Lip blush" is a really
good way to describe it,

01:01:33.556 --> 01:01:35.792
because it makes your lips look so rosy.

01:01:35.792 --> 01:01:38.961
The actual balm formula is
really nice and hydrating,

01:01:38.961 --> 01:01:42.498
but no one on planet Earth
needs a $58 lip balm.

01:01:42.498 --> 01:01:43.599
This is cute, though.

01:01:43.599 --> 01:01:46.135
Holo Taco polishes have been super popular

01:01:46.135 --> 01:01:47.203
since they were released,

01:01:47.203 --> 01:01:49.272
but I've actually never tried them.

01:01:49.272 --> 01:01:51.874
I picked up a few different
formulas to test out.

01:01:51.874 --> 01:01:53.443
I really did not like

01:01:53.443 --> 01:01:55.311
the skinny brushes these came with,

01:01:55.311 --> 01:01:57.513
but they actually sell
wide brush replacements,

01:01:57.513 --> 01:01:59.082
so I just swapped them all out.

01:01:59.082 --> 01:02:01.718
This cream shade I tried
first was so full-coverage

01:02:01.718 --> 01:02:03.186
and applied really smoothly.

01:02:03.186 --> 01:02:05.054
The color was just so rich.

01:02:05.054 --> 01:02:06.923
I got this iridescent flaky topper,

01:02:06.923 --> 01:02:09.192
and I was surprised at
how much I liked it.

01:02:09.192 --> 01:02:10.993
I don't really do toppers, but this one

01:02:10.993 --> 01:02:13.663
looks so shifty and cool on the nails.

01:02:13.663 --> 01:02:16.466
I obviously had to test out
some holographic polishes.

01:02:16.466 --> 01:02:18.468
Both of these also applied really well

01:02:18.468 --> 01:02:20.303
and had amazing color payoff.

01:02:20.303 --> 01:02:21.571
I had to turn my flashlight on

01:02:21.571 --> 01:02:23.439
so you could really see the holo.

01:02:23.439 --> 01:02:25.475
I applied the Super Glossy Topcoat

01:02:25.475 --> 01:02:28.611
on all of these formulas,
and I really loved it.

01:02:28.611 --> 01:02:30.213
I like it when my topcoat

01:02:30.213 --> 01:02:31.781
has an almost plumping effect,

01:02:31.781 --> 01:02:34.250
where it makes regular
polish kind of look like gel,

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:37.487
and this did that while making
the manicure super shiny.

01:02:37.487 --> 01:02:39.922
Overall, I'm really happy
with all the shades I got,

01:02:39.922 --> 01:02:41.190
and I can't wait to try more.

01:02:41.190 --> 01:02:43.793
This is the Milani Daze
of Disco Shimmer Spray.

01:02:43.793 --> 01:02:46.929
It's supposed to be a holographic
glitter setting spray,

01:02:46.929 --> 01:02:49.265
but I was seeing absolutely no glitter

01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:50.967
when I sprayed some on my hand.

01:02:50.967 --> 01:02:53.803
And I shook this really
well, like for a full minute.

01:02:53.803 --> 01:02:55.271
I sprayed it all over my face,

01:02:55.271 --> 01:02:57.940
and it did make my skin
look extremely dewy,

01:02:57.940 --> 01:03:00.743
but I still wasn't really
seeing the glitter effect.

01:03:00.743 --> 01:03:02.378
I could only see if I was looking

01:03:02.378 --> 01:03:04.280
really, really, really closely.

01:03:04.280 --> 01:03:06.916
The glitter effect is
definitely not as noticeable

01:03:06.916 --> 01:03:08.084
as I thought it was going to be,

01:03:08.084 --> 01:03:09.685
and the actual setting-spray formula

01:03:09.685 --> 01:03:11.554
just made me look oily.

01:03:11.554 --> 01:03:13.756
This month, I tested out a lot of products

01:03:13.756 --> 01:03:15.224
from Simihaze Beauty.

01:03:15.224 --> 01:03:16.459
This is a new brand for me,

01:03:16.459 --> 01:03:18.561
so let's start with the stuff I liked.

01:03:18.561 --> 01:03:20.596
The Solar Tint blush duo comes with

01:03:20.596 --> 01:03:22.832
a cheek pigment and a cheek gloss.

01:03:22.832 --> 01:03:24.433
These both went on really easily,

01:03:24.433 --> 01:03:26.269
and the pigment is so good.

01:03:26.269 --> 01:03:28.971
Surprisingly, I loved
the cheek gloss more,

01:03:28.971 --> 01:03:32.241
even though it's not super
practical for all-day wear.

01:03:32.241 --> 01:03:34.677
I didn't love the color
of this Velvet Blur

01:03:34.677 --> 01:03:36.746
matte lip balm on my skin tone,

01:03:36.746 --> 01:03:39.048
but the formula itself was so good.

01:03:39.048 --> 01:03:40.583
It has the comfort of a lip balm

01:03:40.583 --> 01:03:43.486
but the pigment and blurring
effect of a matte lipstick.

01:03:43.486 --> 01:03:45.788
It's creamy and super comfortable.

01:03:45.788 --> 01:03:47.323
I thought the Lunar lip gel

01:03:47.323 --> 01:03:50.493
and the Super Slick mini
lip balm were just OK.

01:03:50.493 --> 01:03:51.794
The lip gel was pretty,

01:03:51.794 --> 01:03:53.629
but the formula was nothing special.

01:03:53.629 --> 01:03:55.798
It's just a thin lip gloss.

01:03:55.798 --> 01:03:57.900
The mini lip balm was pretty moisturizing,

01:03:57.900 --> 01:03:59.202
and the tint is cute,

01:03:59.202 --> 01:04:01.671
but it's so little
product for what you pay.

01:04:01.671 --> 01:04:03.272
Again, nothing special.

01:04:03.272 --> 01:04:05.474
Now for the products I just didn't like.

01:04:05.474 --> 01:04:08.411
I wanted to love the Sun
Flush all-over face tint,

01:04:08.411 --> 01:04:10.513
but it just ended up being really patchy

01:04:10.513 --> 01:04:12.648
and broke up my foundation.

01:04:12.648 --> 01:04:14.383
And I tried this a few different ways

01:04:14.383 --> 01:04:16.352
to see if I was just applying it wrong,

01:04:16.352 --> 01:04:18.754
but it still messed up
my foundation underneath.

01:04:18.754 --> 01:04:20.656
The Easy Lash Clean Lift mascara

01:04:20.656 --> 01:04:22.491
just didn't do much for my lashes.

01:04:22.491 --> 01:04:23.559
I didn't get much lift,

01:04:23.559 --> 01:04:25.094
I got little to no volume,

01:04:25.094 --> 01:04:27.063
and my lashes weren't
lengthened very much.

01:04:27.063 --> 01:04:29.699
Overall, I love the
packaging of this brand,

01:04:29.699 --> 01:04:31.434
and it does have some standout products,

01:04:31.434 --> 01:04:33.236
but I think it's all very overpriced

01:04:33.236 --> 01:04:35.538
for how the actual formulas perform.

01:04:35.538 --> 01:04:37.006
Everyone has been raving

01:04:37.006 --> 01:04:39.308
about the Summer Fridays Lip Butter Balms.

01:04:39.308 --> 01:04:41.611
This set with the minis
is limited-edition,

01:04:41.611 --> 01:04:44.146
but they sell all of
these shades in full size.

01:04:44.146 --> 01:04:46.449
I ended up really enjoying these.

01:04:46.449 --> 01:04:48.417
The formula is on the thicker side,

01:04:48.417 --> 01:04:49.518
but not sticky.

01:04:49.518 --> 01:04:51.120
They feel really moisturizing,

01:04:51.120 --> 01:04:54.156
and I like how they give
an almost lip-gloss effect.

01:04:54.156 --> 01:04:55.725
I loved all of the tinted balms,

01:04:55.725 --> 01:04:57.960
but I think Poppy was my favorite.

01:04:57.960 --> 01:05:00.463
They all give a pretty,
subtle wash of color,

01:05:00.463 --> 01:05:02.198
and they have this nice vanilla scent

01:05:02.198 --> 01:05:03.599
that's not overpowering.

01:05:03.599 --> 01:05:05.034
I'm obsessed with these.

01:05:05.034 --> 01:05:06.969
This is the Danessa Myricks Beauty

01:05:06.969 --> 01:05:09.472
Lightwork IV Transcendence palette.

01:05:09.472 --> 01:05:10.539
I'm not gonna lie,

01:05:10.539 --> 01:05:13.943
I was very intimidated
by this palette at first.

01:05:13.943 --> 01:05:15.845
It has four different formulas:

01:05:15.845 --> 01:05:18.514
velvet chromes, which are
color-shifting powders;

01:05:18.514 --> 01:05:21.350
pressed chrome flakes,
which are flaky toppers;

01:05:21.350 --> 01:05:24.220
glass metallics, which are
super-reflective powders;

01:05:24.220 --> 01:05:26.522
and aqua chromes, which
are water-activated

01:05:26.522 --> 01:05:28.124
duo-chrome pigments.

01:05:28.124 --> 01:05:30.092
So there is a lot going on.

01:05:30.092 --> 01:05:32.361
I started applying over a light wash

01:05:32.361 --> 01:05:35.131
of black eye-shadow base to
make the colors pop more,

01:05:35.131 --> 01:05:37.566
but I don't even think
I needed to do that,

01:05:37.566 --> 01:05:40.703
because these powders are so pigmented.

01:05:40.703 --> 01:05:43.139
I was determined to use all
of the different formulas,

01:05:43.139 --> 01:05:46.075
so I added one of the
metallics in the inner corners

01:05:46.075 --> 01:05:48.077
and put the chrome flakes in the center.

01:05:48.077 --> 01:05:49.612
The flakes were the only formula

01:05:49.612 --> 01:05:51.247
that was a little difficult to work with,

01:05:51.247 --> 01:05:54.083
only because they're kind of
hard to pick up and apply,

01:05:54.083 --> 01:05:56.185
but I think they added
a really cool texture

01:05:56.185 --> 01:05:58.020
and color shift to the eye look.

01:05:58.020 --> 01:05:59.789
I used an aqua chrome for some eyeliner,

01:05:59.789 --> 01:06:01.891
and it's so reflective and sparkly,

01:06:01.891 --> 01:06:03.192
and it dried down quickly.

01:06:03.192 --> 01:06:06.028
This palette is extremely pricey,

01:06:06.028 --> 01:06:07.897
and I did get some slight fallout,

01:06:07.897 --> 01:06:09.899
but the quality is definitely there,

01:06:09.899 --> 01:06:12.835
and I think it's so much
more versatile than it seems.

01:06:12.835 --> 01:06:15.104
The shades in here are so transformative

01:06:15.104 --> 01:06:17.406
and really inspire you
to play with your makeup.

01:06:17.406 --> 01:06:19.442
Plus, it can also be used on the face.

01:06:19.442 --> 01:06:21.177
These are the L'Oréal Colour Riche

01:06:21.177 --> 01:06:23.112
Intense Volume matte lipsticks.

01:06:23.112 --> 01:06:24.714
I thought these were going to be similar

01:06:24.714 --> 01:06:27.416
to the Nars Powermatte
lipstick I tried a while ago,

01:06:27.416 --> 01:06:28.985
but the formula is different.

01:06:28.985 --> 01:06:31.554
The color payoff on these is so good,

01:06:31.554 --> 01:06:33.389
and they apply really smoothly.

01:06:33.389 --> 01:06:35.891
This is one of the most
comfortable matte formulas

01:06:35.891 --> 01:06:38.828
I've ever tried, especially
from the drugstore.

01:06:38.828 --> 01:06:41.130
What makes this lipstick
different from the Nars one

01:06:41.130 --> 01:06:44.033
is that it's unfortunately
not transfer-proof.

01:06:44.033 --> 01:06:46.168
To be fair, it claims to be smudge-proof,

01:06:46.168 --> 01:06:47.670
so it's not the same thing.

01:06:47.670 --> 01:06:49.438
Regardless, I think these lipsticks

01:06:49.438 --> 01:06:50.706
are comfortable on the lips,

01:06:50.706 --> 01:06:52.341
and the colors are so rich,

01:06:52.341 --> 01:06:54.243
so I really like them.

01:06:54.243 --> 01:06:56.812
Apparently Gwen Stefani
has her own beauty brand

01:06:56.812 --> 01:06:59.415
called GXVE, and this is
the first product from it

01:06:59.415 --> 01:07:00.916
that I've ever tried.

01:07:00.916 --> 01:07:04.153
This is the Double Dippin'
2-1 lip color remover

01:07:04.153 --> 01:07:05.788
and hydrating lip mask.

01:07:05.788 --> 01:07:08.324
I wanted to test it out with
my Nars Powermatte lipstick,

01:07:08.324 --> 01:07:11.060
since it's one of my
hardest-to-remove lipsticks.

01:07:11.060 --> 01:07:13.262
The formula of this lip mask feels

01:07:13.262 --> 01:07:15.464
like a makeup-removing cleansing balm.

01:07:15.464 --> 01:07:18.334
If you've never tried one,
they feel really oily.

01:07:18.334 --> 01:07:19.502
Because of that, it actually

01:07:19.502 --> 01:07:21.170
broke the lipstick down really well.

01:07:21.170 --> 01:07:23.105
It made it super easy to remove.

01:07:23.105 --> 01:07:26.008
However, as a regular
lip mask, it just feels

01:07:26.008 --> 01:07:29.345
way too oily and thin to be comfortable.

01:07:29.345 --> 01:07:31.113
This just feels like one of those products

01:07:31.113 --> 01:07:32.548
that they market as multiuse

01:07:32.548 --> 01:07:34.116
to make it sound more innovative.

01:07:34.116 --> 01:07:36.085
Lights Lacquer just released
its winter collection,

01:07:36.085 --> 01:07:37.319
called Cocktail Hour.

01:07:37.319 --> 01:07:39.021
I do own a lot of their polishes,

01:07:39.021 --> 01:07:40.856
so this isn't a new brand for me,

01:07:40.856 --> 01:07:42.625
but I definitely think this is my favorite

01:07:42.625 --> 01:07:44.693
color story they've ever done.

01:07:44.693 --> 01:07:46.962
The polishes have those wide, flat brushes

01:07:46.962 --> 01:07:48.197
I love for applying.

01:07:48.197 --> 01:07:50.666
It just makes it so
much easier and faster.

01:07:50.666 --> 01:07:51.834
I tried the cream shades,

01:07:51.834 --> 01:07:53.569
Old Money and Audrey, first,

01:07:53.569 --> 01:07:55.504
and both were full coverage in two coats,

01:07:55.504 --> 01:07:57.907
and the application was really smooth.

01:07:57.907 --> 01:08:00.142
Then I tried the jelly
shade, called Lady in Red.

01:08:00.142 --> 01:08:01.444
Because this is a jelly,

01:08:01.444 --> 01:08:03.045
it's way more sheer than a cream,

01:08:03.045 --> 01:08:04.847
so I ended up doing two thicker coats

01:08:04.847 --> 01:08:06.015
for full color payoff.

01:08:06.015 --> 01:08:08.184
The color is slightly lighter on my nails

01:08:08.184 --> 01:08:11.153
than in the bottle, but
still pretty and so shiny.

01:08:11.153 --> 01:08:14.123
Next I tried To the Nines,
which is a metallic polish.

01:08:14.123 --> 01:08:15.758
I really love this color,

01:08:15.758 --> 01:08:18.094
but this formula is
probably the least forgiving

01:08:18.094 --> 01:08:20.062
when it comes to streaks and bubbles.

01:08:20.062 --> 01:08:22.665
My two absolute favorite
shades from the collection

01:08:22.665 --> 01:08:25.067
are Whiskey Neat and Diamonds Are Forever.

01:08:25.067 --> 01:08:27.203
Whiskey Neat is also a metallic formula,

01:08:27.203 --> 01:08:28.838
but it's more of a duo-chrome,

01:08:28.838 --> 01:08:31.140
and Diamonds Are Forever
is like a milky taupe

01:08:31.140 --> 01:08:33.209
with a bunch of superfine glitter in it.

01:08:33.209 --> 01:08:35.945
I don't think these colors
separately are anything new,

01:08:35.945 --> 01:08:38.314
but I love how they all work
together in this collection,

01:08:38.314 --> 01:08:40.316
and the formulas are all so good.

01:08:40.316 --> 01:08:44.854
We have yet another
color-changing product to review.

01:08:44.854 --> 01:08:46.388
This is the Kylie Cosmetics

01:08:46.388 --> 01:08:48.090
transformative liquid lip tint

01:08:48.090 --> 01:08:50.960
that was a part of her
collab with the Wizard of Oz.

01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:53.662
It goes from emerald green to pink.

01:08:53.662 --> 01:08:54.930
The smell is interesting.

01:08:54.930 --> 01:08:57.733
It kind of smells like an apple-y shampoo.

01:08:57.733 --> 01:08:59.368
The formula is pretty thin.

01:08:59.368 --> 01:09:01.470
I do like this giant doe-foot applicator.

01:09:01.470 --> 01:09:03.472
The color is actually a little more unique

01:09:03.472 --> 01:09:05.841
than other color-changing
lip products I've tried.

01:09:05.841 --> 01:09:07.776
The pink was a bit deeper and I think

01:09:07.776 --> 01:09:09.512
more flattering on my skin tone.

01:09:09.512 --> 01:09:10.946
I would wear this again because

01:09:10.946 --> 01:09:12.848
the stain it leaves behind is pretty,

01:09:12.848 --> 01:09:14.917
but I do wish the formula was thicker.

01:09:14.917 --> 01:09:16.952
These are the Fleeky Friday Cosmetics

01:09:16.952 --> 01:09:18.654
Crystal Crease eyeliners.

01:09:18.654 --> 01:09:21.490
These are handmade
reusable crystal eyeliners

01:09:21.490 --> 01:09:23.159
that you apply with lash glue.

01:09:23.159 --> 01:09:24.260
It was a little hard for me

01:09:24.260 --> 01:09:25.761
to get them in a comfortable spot,

01:09:25.761 --> 01:09:27.263
because I have hooded lids.

01:09:27.263 --> 01:09:29.198
You can cut these to fit
your eye shape better,

01:09:29.198 --> 01:09:30.533
so I'm going to do that next time,

01:09:30.533 --> 01:09:32.334
but I think these are so fun.

01:09:32.334 --> 01:09:34.270
They look like you just did so much work

01:09:34.270 --> 01:09:36.605
applying each individual rhinestone.

01:09:36.605 --> 01:09:38.941
Cirque Colors is one of my
favorite nail-polish brands,

01:09:38.941 --> 01:09:40.976
and they just dropped
their holiday collection.

01:09:40.976 --> 01:09:44.013
I love that they have a spin
on the classic red and green,

01:09:44.013 --> 01:09:45.514
this mix of pearly shades,

01:09:45.514 --> 01:09:47.783
and then this more unique duochrome.

01:09:47.783 --> 01:09:51.120
Sashay reminds me of red
bows and Christmas ornaments.

01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:53.155
To me it leans more pink than red,

01:09:53.155 --> 01:09:54.390
but it's still beautiful.

01:09:54.390 --> 01:09:56.392
Verdigris Jelly is a jelly polish.

01:09:56.392 --> 01:09:58.227
It is more sheer because it's a jelly,

01:09:58.227 --> 01:10:01.363
so I did three layers,
and it looked so shiny.

01:10:01.363 --> 01:10:02.731
My favorite shade in the collection

01:10:02.731 --> 01:10:04.333
is definitely Tahitian Pearl,

01:10:04.333 --> 01:10:06.035
which is this dark duochrome

01:10:06.035 --> 01:10:07.903
that shifts from pink to green,

01:10:07.903 --> 01:10:10.005
and it has this holographic glitter in it.

01:10:10.005 --> 01:10:11.607
I did three coats for this one too

01:10:11.607 --> 01:10:13.342
because it showed the color shift better,

01:10:13.342 --> 01:10:15.477
and I think it made the glitter pop more.

01:10:15.477 --> 01:10:16.812
This is a really unique color,

01:10:16.812 --> 01:10:18.547
and I can see myself wearing it a lot.

01:10:18.547 --> 01:10:21.584
The last three shades are all
a pearlescent, sheer white

01:10:21.584 --> 01:10:23.352
with different-colored shimmers.

01:10:23.352 --> 01:10:25.154
Serenity has a green shimmer,

01:10:25.154 --> 01:10:27.189
Soleil has a pinky-red shimmer,

01:10:27.189 --> 01:10:29.091
and Siren has a purple shimmer.

01:10:29.091 --> 01:10:30.092
These are all really pretty,

01:10:30.092 --> 01:10:31.660
but you definitely don't need all of them,

01:10:31.660 --> 01:10:32.928
because they're so similar.

01:10:32.928 --> 01:10:35.097
This entire collection
applied really smoothly,

01:10:35.097 --> 01:10:36.932
and even though some shades
had to be layered up,

01:10:36.932 --> 01:10:38.767
I was happy with how they all turned out.

01:10:38.767 --> 01:10:41.937
This is the Half Magic
Magic Flik liquid eyeliner.

01:10:41.937 --> 01:10:45.107
It has this really interesting
tip that's paddle-shaped

01:10:45.107 --> 01:10:47.376
so you can draw fine lines with the edge

01:10:47.376 --> 01:10:49.445
and then fill in with the wide side.

01:10:49.445 --> 01:10:51.113
I suck at eyeliner, but this shape

01:10:51.113 --> 01:10:53.649
actually really helped
me draw the wing easily.

01:10:53.649 --> 01:10:56.518
I will say that I think
the actual eyeliner formula

01:10:56.518 --> 01:10:57.686
is not the best.

01:10:57.686 --> 01:11:00.656
The black isn't super
pigmented like I would prefer,

01:11:00.656 --> 01:11:02.558
but I really liked this tip shape.

01:11:02.558 --> 01:11:05.628
This is the KVD Dazzle
Long-Wear Eyeshadow Stick.

01:11:05.628 --> 01:11:08.297
It's supposed to be a
one-and-done-type product,

01:11:08.297 --> 01:11:09.832
so you don't need primer.

01:11:09.832 --> 01:11:11.700
You just swipe it on and blend.

01:11:11.700 --> 01:11:14.503
I was really surprised at
how soft this formula is.

01:11:14.503 --> 01:11:16.138
It's actually a little too soft,

01:11:16.138 --> 01:11:17.606
like, you have to be gentle with it,

01:11:17.606 --> 01:11:19.608
but it really does glide on easily.

01:11:19.608 --> 01:11:21.710
This is packed with glitter and shimmer,

01:11:21.710 --> 01:11:23.712
and it just looks so pretty on the eyes.

01:11:23.712 --> 01:11:24.980
It's like a way to do glitter

01:11:24.980 --> 01:11:27.016
without any of the mess. I'm a fan.

01:11:27.016 --> 01:11:30.119
I tried a couple products from
the K-beauty brand Romand.

01:11:30.119 --> 01:11:32.087
This glitter palette has been raved about,

01:11:32.087 --> 01:11:34.156
so I was really excited to play with it.

01:11:34.156 --> 01:11:36.392
The shades are meant to be on the softer,

01:11:36.392 --> 01:11:37.760
more translucent side,

01:11:37.760 --> 01:11:39.928
so you can layer them over eye shadow.

01:11:39.928 --> 01:11:42.031
I just applied some of
my blush on the eyes

01:11:42.031 --> 01:11:44.366
and then applied a few
of the shades on top.

01:11:44.366 --> 01:11:45.834
There are shimmer formulas,

01:11:45.834 --> 01:11:48.370
fine glitters, and more chunky glitters.

01:11:48.370 --> 01:11:50.973
Overall, I would say the
formulas are on the dry side,

01:11:50.973 --> 01:11:53.175
but they were actually
pretty easy to work with.

01:11:53.175 --> 01:11:55.611
I had no problem swiping
or patting them on,

01:11:55.611 --> 01:11:57.813
and I had little to no glitter fallout.

01:11:57.813 --> 01:12:00.416
I also tried the Glasting Water Tint.

01:12:00.416 --> 01:12:02.451
The color and gloss are separate layers,

01:12:02.451 --> 01:12:05.888
so you get that long-lasting
tint with a glossy finish.

01:12:05.888 --> 01:12:09.625
These feel so hydrating and
comfortable on the lips.

01:12:09.625 --> 01:12:10.526
They're really lightweight,

01:12:10.526 --> 01:12:12.428
and they definitely do leave a stain.

01:12:12.428 --> 01:12:14.997
Look at my hand after I
wiped those swatches off.

01:12:14.997 --> 01:12:17.599
I've never tried a product
from Jane Iredale before,

01:12:17.599 --> 01:12:18.967
but this one intrigued me.

01:12:18.967 --> 01:12:21.236
This is the HydroPure tinted serum.

01:12:21.236 --> 01:12:23.539
It's a serum with a bunch
of pigment beads inside

01:12:23.539 --> 01:12:25.574
that are meant to give you light coverage.

01:12:25.574 --> 01:12:27.710
You're supposed to mix this
with your fingers first

01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:28.744
to break up the beads,

01:12:28.744 --> 01:12:30.446
then apply with your fingers.

01:12:30.446 --> 01:12:33.615
I really don't like finger
applications for foundations,

01:12:33.615 --> 01:12:36.318
but it really was the best
way to apply this product.

01:12:36.318 --> 01:12:37.353
It did not look great

01:12:37.353 --> 01:12:39.588
when I tried it with
a brush and my sponge.

01:12:39.588 --> 01:12:41.457
The coverage is definitely light.

01:12:41.457 --> 01:12:43.992
I feel like it looked like
I had no makeup on at all.

01:12:43.992 --> 01:12:46.061
I was hoping it would feel moisturizing,

01:12:46.061 --> 01:12:48.464
but it felt like nothing on my skin.

01:12:48.464 --> 01:12:50.799
All my other makeup went
on top of this just fine,

01:12:50.799 --> 01:12:52.935
and I really liked how
my skin was looking.

01:12:52.935 --> 01:12:55.170
It's so expensive, but
I think this is great

01:12:55.170 --> 01:12:58.140
for people who want a very
natural-looking skin tint.

01:12:58.140 --> 01:12:59.408
Charlotte Tilbury released

01:12:59.408 --> 01:13:02.144
these Hypnotising Pop Shot single shadows.

01:13:02.144 --> 01:13:04.346
The packaging on this is so cute.

01:13:04.346 --> 01:13:06.849
This is meant to be a
super-glittery, pigmented,

01:13:06.849 --> 01:13:08.417
multidimensional shadow.

01:13:08.417 --> 01:13:09.785
This was really easy to apply.

01:13:09.785 --> 01:13:11.320
I just swiped it on with my finger

01:13:11.320 --> 01:13:13.088
and blended out the edges.

01:13:13.088 --> 01:13:14.690
I did get a tiny bit of fallout,

01:13:14.690 --> 01:13:16.525
but I was able to just brush it away.

01:13:16.525 --> 01:13:18.761
I really love the sparkly,

01:13:18.761 --> 01:13:20.796
shifty effect you get with this formula.

01:13:20.796 --> 01:13:22.631
You can definitely get a similar effect

01:13:22.631 --> 01:13:24.967
with one of those ColourPop
Super Shock shadows,

01:13:24.967 --> 01:13:27.569
but this formula is really
beautiful on the eyes.

01:13:27.569 --> 01:13:29.638
Rare Beauty just released a powder version

01:13:29.638 --> 01:13:31.507
of its super-popular highlighters.

01:13:31.507 --> 01:13:33.409
I've been seeing some
conflicting statements

01:13:33.409 --> 01:13:35.844
about whether this product looks glittery.

01:13:35.844 --> 01:13:39.214
There is definitely some
superfine glitter in this formula,

01:13:39.214 --> 01:13:41.683
but I don't think it looks
glittery on the skin.

01:13:41.683 --> 01:13:43.986
The glow is obviously
there, and it's so pretty.

01:13:43.986 --> 01:13:45.521
It's almost wet-looking.

01:13:45.521 --> 01:13:47.856
I actually thought it
emphasized my texture a bit

01:13:47.856 --> 01:13:49.124
when I first tried it.

01:13:49.124 --> 01:13:50.292
When I tried it the second time,

01:13:50.292 --> 01:13:51.894
I just went in with a little less product,

01:13:51.894 --> 01:13:52.995
and it looked better.

01:13:52.995 --> 01:13:54.797
I don't think this is as natural-looking

01:13:54.797 --> 01:13:55.731
as the liquid version,

01:13:55.731 --> 01:13:57.800
but it's still a really nice highlighter.

01:13:57.800 --> 01:13:59.935
I tried a couple new
Fenty products this month:

01:13:59.935 --> 01:14:02.404
the Plush Puddin'
Intensive Recovery lip mask

01:14:02.404 --> 01:14:04.640
and the Glossy Posse Volume 5.0.

01:14:04.640 --> 01:14:06.475
Let's talk about the lip mask first.

01:14:06.475 --> 01:14:08.043
The packaging is really cool.

01:14:08.043 --> 01:14:10.412
You twist it and the product
dispenses from the top,

01:14:10.412 --> 01:14:12.147
so you don't have to dip into it.

01:14:12.147 --> 01:14:15.317
The formula is very thick,
which I personally love.

01:14:15.317 --> 01:14:18.921
It just feels so moisturizing
and plush on the lips.

01:14:18.921 --> 01:14:21.723
It also gave this really nice
shine I wasn't expecting.

01:14:21.723 --> 01:14:23.725
I did wear this lip
mask for a couple nights

01:14:23.725 --> 01:14:25.360
to see if it helped with my dryness,

01:14:25.360 --> 01:14:26.628
and I saw the difference.

01:14:26.628 --> 01:14:28.664
My lips were so much
more soft and hydrated,

01:14:28.664 --> 01:14:30.933
so I am definitely going
to keep using this.

01:14:30.933 --> 01:14:33.669
Now on to the Glossy Posse Volume 5.0.

01:14:33.669 --> 01:14:35.370
Fenty Beauty does these gloss sets

01:14:35.370 --> 01:14:37.139
for the holiday season every year,

01:14:37.139 --> 01:14:39.741
usually with a
limited-edition shade inside.

01:14:39.741 --> 01:14:42.578
This set contains a gloss
bomb cream in Cupcakin',

01:14:42.578 --> 01:14:44.780
a gloss bomb heat in Fenty Glow Heat,

01:14:44.780 --> 01:14:47.516
and a regular gloss bomb in Fuchsia Flex.

01:14:47.516 --> 01:14:49.818
Cupcakin' is a really pigmented gloss,

01:14:49.818 --> 01:14:52.688
and Fenty Glow Heat gives
you that kind of spicy,

01:14:52.688 --> 01:14:54.256
tingly lip plumping.

01:14:54.256 --> 01:14:57.059
Fuchsia Flex is the specific
shade that's been going viral.

01:14:57.059 --> 01:14:59.161
It's Fenty's regular gloss formula

01:14:59.161 --> 01:15:01.129
in this really beautiful deep pink

01:15:01.129 --> 01:15:02.698
that has a ton of glitter in it.

01:15:02.698 --> 01:15:05.267
All of these formulas
feel so good on the lips.

01:15:05.267 --> 01:15:07.669
Fenty does not miss
with its gloss formula.

01:15:07.669 --> 01:15:08.837
People have been raving about

01:15:08.837 --> 01:15:11.206
the Kosas Revealer Concealer forever,

01:15:11.206 --> 01:15:12.708
so I finally got it.

01:15:12.708 --> 01:15:15.711
It's supposed to be medium
coverage and super creamy.

01:15:15.711 --> 01:15:17.579
This concealer was easy to work with

01:15:17.579 --> 01:15:20.516
and blended out so quickly and easily.

01:15:20.516 --> 01:15:22.885
The coverage looked a bit
lighter than medium to me,

01:15:22.885 --> 01:15:24.119
but it covered enough.

01:15:24.119 --> 01:15:25.821
I would go in with a
little more next time,

01:15:25.821 --> 01:15:27.256
but I loved how this looked.

01:15:27.256 --> 01:15:29.391
I also got the Cloud Set setting powder,

01:15:29.391 --> 01:15:30.893
which people also really love.

01:15:30.893 --> 01:15:32.327
I used my puff to apply this,

01:15:32.327 --> 01:15:35.264
and it smoothed everything
out almost instantly.

01:15:35.264 --> 01:15:37.199
I was so impressed by this powder,

01:15:37.199 --> 01:15:39.034
and I usually hate pressed powders.

01:15:39.034 --> 01:15:41.603
I never use them, let
alone to set my concealer,

01:15:41.603 --> 01:15:43.038
but this looked so nice.

01:15:43.038 --> 01:15:44.640
I used it on the rest of my face too,

01:15:44.640 --> 01:15:47.776
and it just gave this
really soft, blurred look.

01:15:47.776 --> 01:15:50.045
It mattified, but not too much.

01:15:50.045 --> 01:15:53.048
I loved these two products,
especially together.

01:15:53.048 --> 01:15:54.716
This is the Hourglass Cosmetics

01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:56.852
Phantom Volumizing glossy balm.

01:15:56.852 --> 01:15:59.321
It's supposed to be a
lip balm, lip plumper,

01:15:59.321 --> 01:16:01.490
and a lip gloss all in one product.

01:16:01.490 --> 01:16:02.524
These applied nicely,

01:16:02.524 --> 01:16:04.826
but because this formula is so fragile,

01:16:04.826 --> 01:16:06.728
it's easy to apply too much.

01:16:06.728 --> 01:16:08.030
I had to smooth the product out

01:16:08.030 --> 01:16:09.431
with my finger a couple times,

01:16:09.431 --> 01:16:11.633
but other than that, I loved these.

01:16:11.633 --> 01:16:14.036
They have this really nice cooling effect.

01:16:14.036 --> 01:16:16.405
They do feel like a
super-moisturizing lip balm,

01:16:16.405 --> 01:16:18.941
and they have this high-shine
finish, like a gloss.

01:16:18.941 --> 01:16:21.076
It didn't do much for
me in terms of plumping,

01:16:21.076 --> 01:16:22.544
so I think if that's the main thing

01:16:22.544 --> 01:16:24.613
you want from a lip
product, don't get this one.

01:16:24.613 --> 01:16:26.949
I did a little haul at ELF,
and I got some new products

01:16:26.949 --> 01:16:28.984
and some products I've
been wanting to try.

01:16:28.984 --> 01:16:31.887
First up is this ELF
luminous putty bronzer.

01:16:31.887 --> 01:16:34.623
This goes from a putty
formula to a powder.

01:16:34.623 --> 01:16:36.692
Up close, you can see a
lot of shimmer in this,

01:16:36.692 --> 01:16:38.660
but it doesn't look that way on the skin.

01:16:38.660 --> 01:16:42.197
This is one of the most blendable
bronzers I've ever tried.

01:16:42.197 --> 01:16:44.600
Like, it takes no time
at all to blend this out,

01:16:44.600 --> 01:16:47.569
and it brings a really
natural warmth to the skin.

01:16:47.569 --> 01:16:48.570
This was so good.

01:16:48.570 --> 01:16:50.539
Next, I tried the Halo Glow powder puff,

01:16:50.539 --> 01:16:52.040
which is always out of stock.

01:16:52.040 --> 01:16:53.308
People love this.

01:16:53.308 --> 01:16:54.977
I thought it wasn't
going to be any different

01:16:54.977 --> 01:16:57.245
to my normal powder puffs, but it is.

01:16:57.245 --> 01:17:00.616
It's much thicker and softer
than these cheap ones I buy.

01:17:00.616 --> 01:17:02.117
It does pick up a lot of product,

01:17:02.117 --> 01:17:04.353
but I just evened it out
on the back of my hand.

01:17:04.353 --> 01:17:07.389
This did such a nice job
of applying my powder.

01:17:07.389 --> 01:17:09.524
Next, I tried the Lash 'N Roll mascara,

01:17:09.524 --> 01:17:12.227
which kind of reminds me
of the Benefit Roller Lash.

01:17:12.227 --> 01:17:14.529
I usually hate silicone-brush mascaras,

01:17:14.529 --> 01:17:16.698
but I actually like how this
one applied the product.

01:17:16.698 --> 01:17:19.034
It felt like it got every single lash.

01:17:19.034 --> 01:17:21.737
My lashes are so straight, but
this gave them a nice curl.

01:17:21.737 --> 01:17:24.673
I wish it thickened my
lashes more, but for 6 bucks,

01:17:24.673 --> 01:17:26.975
this is a really good drugstore mascara.

01:17:26.975 --> 01:17:29.778
The last product I tested
was the glossy lip stain.

01:17:29.778 --> 01:17:32.047
I can't believe I've
never tried these before.

01:17:32.047 --> 01:17:34.182
This formula is so interesting.

01:17:34.182 --> 01:17:36.018
It feels like water on the lips.

01:17:36.018 --> 01:17:38.253
Like, hydrating but also weightless.

01:17:38.253 --> 01:17:39.421
These are a bit patchy.

01:17:39.421 --> 01:17:40.622
There were some areas where it looked

01:17:40.622 --> 01:17:42.357
like the product wasn't sticking.

01:17:42.357 --> 01:17:44.159
After letting the product
sit for a few minutes,

01:17:44.159 --> 01:17:46.828
I removed it, and it definitely
did leave a stain behind,

01:17:46.828 --> 01:17:48.797
but the stain also looked patchy.

01:17:48.797 --> 01:17:51.099
I do like how this
formula feels on the lips,

01:17:51.099 --> 01:17:52.668
but it doesn't apply evenly.

01:17:52.668 --> 01:17:55.237
For the most part, though,
this was a pretty good haul.

